<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt1214" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwB68" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"notelist","href":"./Template:Notelist"},"params":{"refs":{"wt":"{{efn|name=tri-license|[[Mozilla Public License|MPL-1.1]], [[GNU General Public License|GPL-2.0]], [[GNU Lesser General Public License|LGPL-2.1]]}}\n&lt;!--IsGoogleChromeOpenSource defined above because of nested ref tags-->\n{{efn|name=IsMicrosoftEdgeOpenSource|Chromium, on which Microsoft Edge is based, is open source; the features Microsoft adds to Edge are closed-source. See [[Chromium (web browser)]] for more info.}}\n{{efn|name=flock-license|Proprietary as of 3.0.}}\n{{efn|name=browser|Browser.}}\n{{efn|name=webkit|WebKit.}}\n{{efn|name=icab-cost|[[Gratis versus libre|No cost]], with Pro at cost ($20).}}\n{{efn|name=pfn-cost|Subscriptions available for $1/month, $0.25/week, or $0.05/day.}}\n{{efn|name=ie-cost|Included with Windows.}}\n{{efn|name=mosaic-cost|[[Gratis versus libre|No cost]] for non-commercial use.}}\n{{efn|name=NetscapeVersion|There are five different products which all carry the name Netscape: Netscape versions 1 to 4, properly called &apos;&apos;Netscape Navigator&apos;&apos;, was a browser based on the original Netscape engine. Netscape 4 also was available as an [[Internet suite]], properly called &apos;&apos;Netscape Communicator&apos;&apos;. Netscape 6 and 7 was a new [[Internet]] suite based on the [[Gecko (layout engine)|Gecko engine]] and the [[Mozilla]] Application Suite user interface. Netscape 8, properly called &apos;&apos;Netscape Browser&apos;&apos;, was a distinct browser based on Firefox that could use either the Gecko (Firefox) or [[Trident (layout engine)|Trident]] (Internet Explorer) engine. Netscape resumed use of the &apos;&apos;Navigator&apos;&apos; name from &apos;&apos;Netscape Navigator 9.0 beta 1&apos;&apos;. See [[Netscape]] for more info.}}\n{{efn|name=gecko|Gecko.}}\n{{efn|name=browsertrident|Browser &amp; [[Trident (layout engine)|Trident]].}}\n{{efn|name=safari-cost|Included with macOS, iOS and iPadOS.}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1327269900" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt1215" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Reflist/styles.css"}}'>.mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-2{column-width:30em}.mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-3{column-width:25em}body.skin-vector-2022 .mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-2{column-width:27em}body.skin-vector-2022 .mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-3{column-width:22.5em}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=upper-alpha]{list-style-type:upper-alpha}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=upper-roman]{list-style-type:upper-roman}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=lower-alpha]{list-style-type:lower-alpha}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=lower-greek]{list-style-type:lower-greek}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=lower-roman]{list-style-type:lower-roman}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-upper-alpha .references{list-style-type:upper-alpha}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-upper-roman .references{list-style-type:upper-roman}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-lower-alpha .references{list-style-type:lower-alpha}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-lower-greek .references{list-style-type:lower-greek}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-lower-roman .references{list-style-type:lower-roman}</style></span><div about="#mwt1214" id="mwB7A">
<div class="mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns" typeof="mw:Extension/references" about="#mwt1242" id="mwB7E" data-mw='{"name":"references","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha","responsive":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:252}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:253}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:254}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:255}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:256}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:257}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:258}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:259}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:260}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:261}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:262}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:263}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:264}}"}}'><ol class="mw-references references" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwB7I"><li about="#cite_note-tri-license-11" id="cite_note-tri-license-11" data-mw-footnote-number="a"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwB7M"><a href="#cite_ref-tri-license_11-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwB7Q"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwB7U">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-tri-license_11-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwB7Y"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwB7c">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-tri-license_11-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwB7g"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwB7k">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-tri-license_11-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwB7o"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwB7s">4</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-tri-license_11-4" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwB7w"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwB70">5</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-tri-license-11" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla_Public_License" title="Mozilla Public License" id="mwB74">MPL-1.1</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU_General_Public_License" title="GNU General Public License" id="mwB78">GPL-2.0</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU_Lesser_General_Public_License" title="GNU Lesser General Public License" id="mwB8A">LGPL-2.1</a></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IsGoogleChromeOpenSource-14" id="cite_note-IsGoogleChromeOpenSource-14" data-mw-footnote-number="b"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwB8E"><a href="#cite_ref-IsGoogleChromeOpenSource_14-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwB8I"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwB8M">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IsGoogleChromeOpenSource-14" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Chromium, on which Google Chrome is based, is open source; the features Google adds to Chrome (such as H.264 and ACC decoding, built-in Adobe Flash, and an auto-updater system, among other things) are closed-source. See <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chromium_(web_browser)#Differences_from_Google_Chrome" title="Chromium (web browser)" id="mwB8Q">Chromium (web browser) § Differences from Google Chrome</a> and Google Chrome's Terms of Service for more info.<sup about="#mwt164" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-13"}}'><a href="#cite_note-13" id="mwB8U"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwB8Y"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8c">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwB8g">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-25" id="cite_note-25" data-mw-footnote-number="c"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwB8k"><a href="#cite_ref-25" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwB8o"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwB8s">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-25" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">EdgeHTML until 2020.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-26" id="cite_note-26" data-mw-footnote-number="d"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwB8w"><a href="#cite_ref-26" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwB80"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwB84">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-26" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Blink since 2020.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IsMicrosoftEdgeOpenSource-28" id="cite_note-IsMicrosoftEdgeOpenSource-28" data-mw-footnote-number="e"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwB88"><a href="#cite_ref-IsMicrosoftEdgeOpenSource_28-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwB9A"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwB9E">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IsMicrosoftEdgeOpenSource-28" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Chromium, on which Microsoft Edge is based, is open source; the features Microsoft adds to Edge are closed-source. See <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chromium_(web_browser)" title="Chromium (web browser)" id="mwB9I">Chromium (web browser)</a> for more info.</span></li>
