<tr class="sortbottom" id="mwDnA">
<th id="mwDnE">Browser</th>
<th id="mwDnI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bookmark_(digital)" title="Bookmark (digital)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDnM">Bookmark</a> management</th>
<th id="mwDnQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Download_manager" title="Download manager" id="mwDnU">Download management</a></th>
<th id="mwDnY">Password managing<sup about="#mwt2534" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-pwd_142-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"pwd","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-pwd-142"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"pwd"},"1":{"wt":"In many integrated password saving tools there are often leaks that make them unsafe.&lt;ref name=\"eweek\">{{cite web|url=http://www.eweek.com/c/a/Security/Google-Chrome-and-Apple-Safari-Lead-Poor-Showing-by-Browsers-in-Password-Management-Test/|archive-url=https://wayback.archive-it.org/all/20171010105338/http://www.eweek.com/security/test%2Dfinds%2Dgoogle%2Dchrome%2Dapple%2Dsafari%2Dweakest%2Din%2Dbrowser%2Dpassword%2Dmanagement|url-status=dead|archive-date=10 October 2017|title=Test Finds Google Chrome, Apple Safari Weakest in Browser Password Management|last=Prince|first=Brian|date=15 December 2008|publisher=[[eweek]]|access-date=22 May 2009}}&lt;/ref>"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-pwd-142" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDnc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDng"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDnk">[</span>v<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDno">]</span></span></a></sup></th>
<th id="mwDns">History</th>
<th id="mwDnw">Open tabs from previous sessions</th>
<th id="mwDn0">Form managing</th>
<th id="mwDn4"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spell_checker" title="Spell checker" id="mwDn8">Spell checking</a></th>
<th id="mwDoA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Search_engine" title="Search engine" id="mwDoE">Search engine</a> toolbar</th>
<th id="mwDoI">Per-site security configuration</th>
<th id="mwDoM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Privacy_mode" title="Privacy mode" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDoQ">Privacy mode</a></th>
<th id="mwDoU">Auto-updater</th></tr>
</tbody></table>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2544" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDoY" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"notelist","href":"./Template:Notelist"},"params":{"refs":{"wt":"&lt;!--pwd defined above because of nested ref tags-->\n{{efn|name=na-mobile|Not available on &apos;&apos;mobile&apos;&apos;.}}\n{{efn|name=chromePerSite|Starting with version 4, Google Chrome can disable Cookies, Images, JavaScript, Plugins, Popups, and Geolocation individually.}}\n{{efn|name=search-toolbar-merged|Lacks search toolbar, but search URL autocompletion provided via addressbar.}}\n{{efn|name=WindowsUpdate|There is no online update facility built into IE, but it gets updated by [[Windows Update]] when enabled. As of Version 10 automatic silent update is the default setting in Internet Explorer. In Microsoft Edge, the option to disable automatic updates via the about dialog is not included.}}\n{{efn|name=QupForm|Available as a PIM plugin which is disabled by default, but it is part of default installation.}}\n{{efn|name=notification-only|Notification only.}}\n{{efn|name=firefoxPrivateMode|[[Firefox 3#Version 3.5|Firefox 3.5]] adds the &apos;&apos;Privacy mode&apos;&apos;. Older versions of Firefox can use the Stealther extension.}}\n{{efn|name=MozSecSep|[[Mozilla]] based [[Web browser|browsers]] like [[Firefox]], [[SeaMonkey]] and [[Flock (web browser)|Flock]] can handle per-site settings for [[HTTP cookie|cookies]], [[pop-up ad|pop-ups]], [[Add-on (Mozilla)|add-on]] installs and images. For more settings, an add-on is needed&amp;nbsp;~ for example, [[NoScript]].}}\n&lt;!--{{efn|name=IESecSep|[[Internet Explorer]] can handle per-site settings for [[HTTP cookie|cookies]]. Furthermore you can specify \"trusted\" and \"untrusted\" sites and assign pre-set rights to both categories.}} -->\n{{efn|name=IESpelling|[[Internet Explorer 10]] supports spell checking.}}\n{{efn|name=InPrivate|[[Internet Explorer 8]] supports InPrivate Browsing.}}\n{{efn|name=K-MeleonToolbar|Through the Privacy toolbar, K-Meleon Versions 1.5 and 1.6, can individually disable Cookies, Images, JavaScript, Popups, and Plugins (e.g. [[Adobe Flash|Flash]] and Java).}}\n{{efn|name=KonqDownload|For the download manager kdenetwork needs to be installed.}}\n{{efn|name=KonqPerSite|Konqueror can handle per-site settings for [[HTTP cookies|cookies]], pop-ups, [[JavaScript]], [[Java (programming language)|Java]] and [[NPAPI|NPAPI modules]] (e.g. [[Adobe Flash|Flash]]).}}\n{{efn|name=engine-dependent|Depending on user&apos;s choice of rendering engine.}}\n{{efn|name=lynx-spell|Lynx is able to edit text with an external editor, which can provide spell checking.}}\n&lt;!--OmniWebSecSep defined above because of nested ref tags-->\n{{efn|name=OpBookmarks|Opera versions before 15 had bookmarks. Newer Opera versions use a different concept called \"Stash\" instead.}}\n{{efn|name=OpForm|Opera can auto-complete forms with your personal information and website usernames. Also there is extension [https://addons.opera.com/en/extensions/details/autocomplete/ AutoComplete] {{webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140725092954/https://addons.opera.com/en/extensions/details/autocomplete/ |date=25 July 2014 }} which can complete forms with form history.}}\n{{efn|name=patch|Developers distribute patch enabling this functionality.}}\n{{efn|name=external|This functionality is handled via third-party software by browser&apos;s design.}}\n{{efn|name=custom-cookies|This browser allows choosing a custom cookie jar, making cookies from other sessions unavailable to new session.}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1327269900" about="#mwt2545" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Reflist/styles.css"}}'/></span><div about="#mwt2544" id="mwDoc">
<div class="mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns" typeof="mw:Extension/references" about="#mwt2586" id="mwDog" data-mw='{"name":"references","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha","responsive":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:366}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:367}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:368}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:369}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:370}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:371}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:372}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:373}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:374}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:375}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:376}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:377}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:378}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:379}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:380}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:381}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:382}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:383}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:384}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:385}}"}}'><ol class="mw-references references" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDok"><li about="#cite_note-na-mobile-116" id="cite_note-na-mobile-116" data-mw-footnote-number="a"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDoo"><a href="#cite_ref-na-mobile_116-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDos"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDow">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-na-mobile_116-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDo0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDo4">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-na-mobile_116-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDo8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDpA">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-na-mobile-116" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Not available on <i id="mwDpE">mobile</i>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-chromePerSite-118" id="cite_note-chromePerSite-118" data-mw-footnote-number="b"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDpI"><a href="#cite_ref-chromePerSite_118-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDpM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDpQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-chromePerSite-118" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Starting with version 4, Google Chrome can disable Cookies, Images, JavaScript, Plugins, Popups, and Geolocation individually.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-search-toolbar-merged-119" id="cite_note-search-toolbar-merged-119" data-mw-footnote-number="c"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDpU"><a href="#cite_ref-search-toolbar-merged_119-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDpY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDpc">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-search-toolbar-merged_119-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDpg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDpk">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-search-toolbar-merged_119-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDpo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDps">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-search-toolbar-merged-119" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Lacks search toolbar, but search URL autocompletion provided via addressbar.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-WindowsUpdate-120" id="cite_note-WindowsUpdate-120" data-mw-footnote-number="d"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDpw"><a href="#cite_ref-WindowsUpdate_120-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDp0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDp4">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-WindowsUpdate_120-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDp8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDqA">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-WindowsUpdate-120" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">There is no online update facility built into IE, but it gets updated by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_Update" title="Windows Update" id="mwDqE">Windows Update</a> when enabled. As of Version 10 automatic silent update is the default setting in Internet Explorer. In Microsoft Edge, the option to disable automatic updates via the about dialog is not included.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-QupForm-121" id="cite_note-QupForm-121" data-mw-footnote-number="e"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDqI"><a href="#cite_ref-QupForm_121-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDqM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDqQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-QupForm-121" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Available as a PIM plugin which is disabled by default, but it is part of default installation.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-notification-only-122" id="cite_note-notification-only-122" data-mw-footnote-number="f"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDqU"><a href="#cite_ref-notification-only_122-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDqY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDqc">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-notification-only_122-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDqg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDqk">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-notification-only-122" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Notification only.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-firefoxPrivateMode-123" id="cite_note-firefoxPrivateMode-123" data-mw-footnote-number="g"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDqo"><a href="#cite_ref-firefoxPrivateMode_123-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDqs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDqw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-firefoxPrivateMode-123" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefox_3#Version_3.5" title="Firefox 3" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDq0">Firefox 3.5</a> adds the <i id="mwDq4">Privacy mode</i>. Older versions of Firefox can use the Stealther extension.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-MozSecSep-124" id="cite_note-MozSecSep-124" data-mw-footnote-number="h"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDq8"><a href="#cite_ref-MozSecSep_124-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDrA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDrE">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozSecSep_124-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDrI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDrM">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-MozSecSep-124" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla" title="Mozilla" id="mwDrQ">Mozilla</a> based <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browser" title="Web browser" id="mwDrU">browsers</a> like <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefox" title="Firefox" id="mwDrY">Firefox</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SeaMonkey" title="SeaMonkey" id="mwDrc">SeaMonkey</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flock_(web_browser)" title="Flock (web browser)" id="mwDrg">Flock</a> can handle per-site settings for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP_cookie" title="HTTP cookie" id="mwDrk">cookies</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pop-up_ad" title="Pop-up ad" id="mwDro">pop-ups</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Add-on_(Mozilla)" title="Add-on (Mozilla)" id="mwDrs">add-on</a> installs and images. For more settings, an add-on is needed<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwDrw"> </span>~ for example, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NoScript" title="NoScript" id="mwDr0">NoScript</a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IESpelling-125" id="cite_note-IESpelling-125" data-mw-footnote-number="i"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDr4"><a href="#cite_ref-IESpelling_125-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDr8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDsA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IESpelling-125" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Explorer_10" title="Internet Explorer 10" id="mwDsE">Internet Explorer 10</a> supports spell checking.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-InPrivate-126" id="cite_note-InPrivate-126" data-mw-footnote-number="j"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDsI"><a href="#cite_ref-InPrivate_126-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDsM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDsQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-InPrivate-126" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Explorer_8" title="Internet Explorer 8" id="mwDsU">Internet Explorer 8</a> supports InPrivate Browsing.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-K-MeleonToolbar-127" id="cite_note-K-MeleonToolbar-127" data-mw-footnote-number="k"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDsY"><a href="#cite_ref-K-MeleonToolbar_127-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDsc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDsg">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-K-MeleonToolbar_127-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDsk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDso">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-K-MeleonToolbar-127" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Through the Privacy toolbar, K-Meleon Versions 1.5 and 1.6, can individually disable Cookies, Images, JavaScript, Popups, and Plugins (e.g. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe_Flash" title="Adobe Flash" id="mwDss">Flash</a> and Java).</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-KonqDownload-128" id="cite_note-KonqDownload-128" data-mw-footnote-number="l"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDsw"><a href="#cite_ref-KonqDownload_128-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDs0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDs4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-KonqDownload-128" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">For the download manager kdenetwork needs to be installed.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-KonqPerSite-129" id="cite_note-KonqPerSite-129" data-mw-footnote-number="m"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDs8"><a href="#cite_ref-KonqPerSite_129-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDtA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDtE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-KonqPerSite-129" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Konqueror can handle per-site settings for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP_cookies" title="HTTP cookies" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDtI">cookies</a>, pop-ups, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JavaScript" title="JavaScript" id="mwDtM">JavaScript</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Java_(programming_language)" title="Java (programming language)" id="mwDtQ">Java</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NPAPI" title="NPAPI" id="mwDtU">NPAPI modules</a> (e.g. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe_Flash" title="Adobe Flash" id="mwDtY">Flash</a>).</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-engine-dependent-130" id="cite_note-engine-dependent-130" data-mw-footnote-number="n"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDtc"><a href="#cite_ref-engine-dependent_130-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDtg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDtk">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-engine-dependent_130-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDto"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDts">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-engine-dependent_130-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDtw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDt0">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-engine-dependent-130" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Depending on user's choice of rendering engine.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-lynx-spell-132" id="cite_note-lynx-spell-132" data-mw-footnote-number="o"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDt4"><a href="#cite_ref-lynx-spell_132-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDt8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDuA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-lynx-spell-132" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Lynx is able to edit text with an external editor, which can provide spell checking.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-OmniWebSecSep-134" id="cite_note-OmniWebSecSep-134" data-mw-footnote-number="p"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDuE"><a href="#cite_ref-OmniWebSecSep_134-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDuI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDuM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-OmniWebSecSep-134" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">OmniWeb supports per-domain settings of options including support for disabling scripting, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ad_blocking" title="Ad blocking" id="mwDuQ">ad blocking</a>, java and cookies. These settings only work on top level domains.<sup about="#mwt2331" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-OmniWeb_133-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"OmniWeb"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-OmniWeb-133"}}'><a href="#cite_note-OmniWeb-133" id="mwDuU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDuY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDuc">[</span>87<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDug">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-OpBookmarks-135" id="cite_note-OpBookmarks-135" data-mw-footnote-number="q"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDuk"><a href="#cite_ref-OpBookmarks_135-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDuo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDus">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-OpBookmarks-135" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Opera versions before 15 had bookmarks. Newer Opera versions use a different concept called "Stash" instead.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-OpForm-136" id="cite_note-OpForm-136" data-mw-footnote-number="r"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDuw"><a href="#cite_ref-OpForm_136-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDu0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDu4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-OpForm-136" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Opera can auto-complete forms with your personal information and website usernames. Also there is extension <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://addons.opera.com/en/extensions/details/autocomplete/" class="external text" id="mwDu8">AutoComplete</a> <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20140725092954/https://addons.opera.com/en/extensions/details/autocomplete/" class="external text" id="mwDvA">Archived</a> 25 July 2014 at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayback_Machine" title="Wayback Machine" id="mwDvE">Wayback Machine</a><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Webarchive_template_wayback_links" id="mwDvI"/> which can complete forms with form history.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-patch-137" id="cite_note-patch-137" data-mw-footnote-number="s"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDvM"><a href="#cite_ref-patch_137-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDvQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDvU">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-patch_137-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDvY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDvc">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-patch-137" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Developers distribute patch enabling this functionality.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-external-138" id="cite_note-external-138" data-mw-footnote-number="t"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDvg"><a href="#cite_ref-external_138-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDvk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDvo">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-external-138" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">This functionality is handled via third-party software by browser's design.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-custom-cookies-139" id="cite_note-custom-cookies-139" data-mw-footnote-number="u"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDvs"><a href="#cite_ref-custom-cookies_139-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDvw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDv0">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-custom-cookies_139-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDv4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDv8">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-custom-cookies-139" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">This browser allows choosing a custom cookie jar, making cookies from other sessions unavailable to new session.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-pwd-142" id="cite_note-pwd-142" data-mw-footnote-number="v"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwDwA"><a href="#cite_ref-pwd_142-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwDwE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwDwI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-pwd-142" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">In many integrated password saving tools there are often leaks that make them unsafe.<sup about="#mwt2537" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-eweek_141-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"eweek"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-eweek-141"}}'><a href="#cite_note-eweek-141" id="mwDwM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDwQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDwU">[</span>89<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDwY">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
</ol></div></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwDwc" aria-labelledby="Accessibility_features"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Accessibility_features">Accessibility features</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Comparison_of_web_browsers&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: Accessibility features"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwDwg">Information about what common accessibility features are implemented natively (without third-party add-ons). Browsers that do not support <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pop-up_ad" title="Pop-up ad" id="mwDwk">pop-ups</a> have no need for pop-up blocking abilities, so that field is marked as N/A.
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2587" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDwo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sticky header","href":"./Template:Sticky_header"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1305414688" about="#mwt2588" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"template:sticky header/styles.css"}}'/></span>
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt2589" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwDws" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sort-under","href":"./Template:Sort-under"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1303987615" about="#mwt2590" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Template:Sort under/styles.css"}}'/></span></p>
<table class="wikitable sortable sort-under sticky-header" style="font-size: 85%; text-align: center; width: auto;" id="mwDww">
<tbody id="mwDw0"><tr id="mwDw4">
<th style="width:12em" id="mwDw8">Browser</th>
<th id="mwDxA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tab_(interface)" title="Tab (interface)" id="mwDxE">Tabbed browsing</a></th>
<th id="mwDxI"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pop-up_ad" title="Pop-up ad" id="mwDxM">Pop-up</a> blocking<sup about="#mwt2591" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-popupblock_143-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"popupblock","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"html":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"popupblock"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-popupblock-143" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDxQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDxU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxY">[</span>a<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDxc">]</span></span></a></sup></th>
<th id="mwDxg">Auto-play blocking</th>
<th id="mwDxk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Incremental_search" title="Incremental search" id="mwDxo">Incremental search</a></th>
<th id="mwDxs"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ad_filtering" title="Ad filtering" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDxw">Ad filtering</a></th>
<th id="mwDx0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Page_zooming" title="Page zooming" id="mwDx4">Page zooming</a><sup about="#mwt2594" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-PageZooming_144-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"PageZooming","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"html":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"PageZooming"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-PageZooming-144" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDx8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDyA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDyE">[</span>b<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDyI">]</span></span></a></sup></th>
<th id="mwDyM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Full_text_search" title="Full text search" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDyQ">Full text search</a> of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_browsing_history" title="Web browsing history" id="mwDyU">history</a></th>
<th id="mwDyY">Content-<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modal_window" title="Modal window" id="mwDyc">modal</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dialog_box" title="Dialog box" id="mwDyg">dialogs</a><sup about="#mwt2597" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Mozilla_Developer_Network_–_Using_tab-modal_prompts_145-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Mozilla Developer Network – Using tab-modal prompts","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"html":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"Mozilla Developer Network – Using tab-modal prompts"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-Mozilla_Developer_Network_–_Using_tab-modal_prompts-145" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwDyk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDyo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDys">[</span>c<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDyw">]</span></span></a></sup></th>
<th id="mwDy0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canvas_fingerprinting" title="Canvas fingerprinting" id="mwDy4">Canvas fingerprinting</a> protection</th></tr>
<tr id="mwDy8">
<th style="background: #F4E3FF; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: left; font-weight: bolder; " scope="row" class="rh heading table-rh" about="#mwt2602" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" id="mwDzE" data-mw='{"attribs":[[{"txt":"style","html":"&lt;span about=\"#mwt2601\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDzA\" data-mw=&apos;{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"rh2\",\"href\":\"./Template:Rh2\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}&apos;>style=\"background: &lt;/span>&lt;span typeof=\"mw:Nowiki\" about=\"#mwt2601\">#F4E3FF&lt;/span>&lt;span about=\"#mwt2601\">; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: left; font-weight: bolder; \" scope=\"row\" class=\"rh heading table-rh\"&lt;/span>"},{"html":""}]]}'><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amaya_(web_browser)" title="Amaya (web browser)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwDzI">Amaya</a></th>
