</tbody></table>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3261" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwElw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"notelist","href":"./Template:Notelist"},"params":{"refs":{"wt":"{{efn|name=popupblock|A more complete list of Pop-Up blockers and addons / programs are in the following article [[List of pop-up blocking software]].}}\n{{efn|name=PageZooming|Page zooming is different from text resizing, as it resizes not only characters, but also multimedia objects and web page layout.}}\n{{efn|name=EpiphanyAdBlock|Epiphany supports [[AdBlock]] as an official extension, in the [[epiphany-extensions]] package.}}\n{{efn|name=FilterINI|Opera 9 introduced a content blocker for webpages ({{webarchive |url=https://web.archive.org/web/20060209045028/http://labs.opera.com/news/2006/02/07/2/ |date=9 February 2006 }}). Earlier releases support [[Wildcard character|wildcard]] [[Protocol (computing)|protocol]]/domain/path and filetype blocking using a filter.ini file. ({{cite web |url=http://www.schrode.net/opera/url_filtering/ |title=Opera browser: Blocking unwanted ads and other cr*p using URL filtering |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://archive.today/20130112054413/http://www.schrode.net/opera/url_filtering/ |archive-date=12 January 2013 |access-date=12 April 2017  }}) More advanced Ad filtering for Opera can also be done with external software.}}\n← ! deleted link to an unrelated commercial website -->\n{{efn|name=QupNonBlock|Requires building with \"NONBLOCK_JS_DIALOGS\" compile flag enabled; may cause crashes: {{Deprecated archive|url=https://archive.today/20140203062255/https://github.com/QupZilla/qupzilla/blob/master/BUILDING}}.}}\n{{efn|name=AdBlock|Most [[Gecko (layout engine)|Gecko]] browsers have options to block chosen images and cookies. Extended Ad filter support can be added by installing an extension such as [[Adblock Plus]].}}\n{{efn|name=GoogleChromeUpdate|Feature was intentionally removed via regular patch update, due to poor impact on performance.}}{{cite web|url=https://productforums.google.com/forum/#!msg/chrome/1uK-7tWOe_o/G9Q12DahJRAJ |title=Chrome full text history search |publisher=Google Chrome Help Forum |date=24 September 2013 |access-date=5 September 2017}}\n{{efn|name=SafariPopupBlock|Does not allow selective blocking of pop-ups. Safari can only block all pop-ups, or none.}}\n{{efn|name=SafariAdblocking|Ad filter support can be added by installing extensions.{{webarchive |url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080701200839/http://pimpmysafari.com/plugins/?c=Adblocking |date=1 July 2008 }}}}\n{{efn|name=IE6Tab|IE6 had no &apos;&apos;tabbed browsing&apos;&apos; support.}}\n{{efn|name=IE6Popup|IE6 included pop-up blocking with Windows XP Service Pack 2 [https://www.microsoft.com/WindowsXP/using/web/sp2_popupblocker.mspx]}}\n{{efn|name=iPhoneZoom|Page zooming supported in the iPhone version of Safari. Screen zooming is built into [[macOS]].}}\n{{efn|name=Spotlight|Full-text history search is available through [[Spotlight (software)|Spotlight]], a feature of the macOS operating system.}}\n{{efn|name=Mozilla Developer Network – Using tab-modal prompts|{{cite web |url=https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Using_tab-modal_prompts |title=Mozilla Developer Network – Using tab-modal prompts |publisher=Developer.mozilla.org |date=3 February 2011 |access-date=23 May 2012 |archive-date=19 October 2012 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121019133659/https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Using_tab-modal_prompts |url-status=dead }}}}\n{{efn|name=Firefox Content-modal dialogs|{{cite web|url=https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=59314 |title=Bug 59314 – JavaScript alerts should be content-modal, not window-modal |publisher=Bugzilla.mozilla.org |access-date=23 May 2012}}}}\n{{efn|name=ChromePopup|The option \"Do not allow any site to show pop-ups\" in Google Chrome, which is the default, actually allows sites to show pop-ups which are not considered harmful.}}\n{{efn|name=text-modal-dialogs|Although text browsers don&apos;t have dialog windows, their prompts behave as modal dialogs – block the input until answer is received.}}\n{{efn|name=external|This functionality is handled by third-party software by browser&apos;s design.}}\n&lt;!--IEHistorySearch defined above because of nested ref tags-->"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1327269900" about="#mwt3262" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Reflist/styles.css"}}'/></span><div about="#mwt3261" id="mwEl0">
<div class="mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns" typeof="mw:Extension/references" about="#mwt3307" id="mwEl4" data-mw='{"name":"references","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha","responsive":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:452}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:453}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:454}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:455}}\n← ! deleted link to an unrelated commercial website -->\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:456}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:457}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:458}}{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:459}}&lt;cite class=\"citation web cs1\">[https://productforums.google.com/forum/#!msg/chrome/1uK-7tWOe_o/G9Q12DahJRAJ \"Chrome full text history search\"]. Google Chrome Help Forum. 24 September 2013&lt;span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved &lt;span class=\"nowrap\">5 September&lt;/span> 2017&lt;/span>.&lt;/cite>&lt;span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Chrome+full+text+history+search&amp;rft.pub=Google+Chrome+Help+Forum&amp;rft.date=2013-09-24&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fproductforums.google.com%2Fforum%2F%23%21msg%2Fchrome%2F1uK-7tWOe_o%2FG9Q12DahJRAJ&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AComparison+of+web+browsers\" class=\"Z3988\">&lt;/span>\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:460}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:461}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:462}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:463}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:464}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:465}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:466}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:467}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:468}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:469}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:470}}"}}'><ol class="mw-references references" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEl8"><li about="#cite_note-popupblock-143" id="cite_note-popupblock-143" data-mw-footnote-number="a"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEmA"><a href="#cite_ref-popupblock_143-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEmE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEmI">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-popupblock_143-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEmM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEmQ">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-popupblock-143" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">A more complete list of Pop-Up blockers and addons / programs are in the following article <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_pop-up_blocking_software" title="List of pop-up blocking software" id="mwEmU">List of pop-up blocking software</a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-PageZooming-144" id="cite_note-PageZooming-144" data-mw-footnote-number="b"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEmY"><a href="#cite_ref-PageZooming_144-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEmc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEmg">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-PageZooming_144-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEmk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEmo">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-PageZooming-144" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Page zooming is different from text resizing, as it resizes not only characters, but also multimedia objects and web page layout.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Mozilla_Developer_Network_–_Using_tab-modal_prompts-145" id="cite_note-Mozilla_Developer_Network_–_Using_tab-modal_prompts-145" data-mw-footnote-number="c"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEms"><a href="#cite_ref-Mozilla_Developer_Network_–_Using_tab-modal_prompts_145-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEmw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEm0">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-Mozilla_Developer_Network_–_Using_tab-modal_prompts_145-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEm4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEm8">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Mozilla_Developer_Network_–_Using_tab-modal_prompts-145" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha"><style data-mw-deduplicate="TemplateStyles:r1333433106" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" about="#mwt3293" id="mwEnA" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'>.mw-parser-output cite.citation{font-style:inherit;word-wrap:break-word}.mw-parser-output .citation q{quotes:"\"""\"""'""'"}.mw-parser-output .citation:target{background-color:rgba(0,127,255,0.133)}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-free.id-lock-free a{background:url("//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/65/Lock-green.svg")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-limited.id-lock-limited a,.mw-parser-output .id-lock-registration.id-lock-registration a{background:url("//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d6/Lock-gray-alt-2.svg")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .id-lock-subscription.id-lock-subscription a{background:url("//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/aa/Lock-red-alt-2.svg")right 0.1em center/9px no-repeat}.mw-parser-output .cs1-ws-icon a{background:url("//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4c/Wikisource-logo.svg")right 0.1em center/12px no-repeat}body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .id-lock-free a,body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .id-lock-limited a,body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .id-lock-registration a,body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .id-lock-subscription a,body:not(.skin-timeless):not(.skin-minerva) .mw-parser-output .cs1-ws-icon a{background-size:contain;padding:0 1em 0 0}.mw-parser-output .cs1-code{color:inherit;background:inherit;border:none;padding:inherit}.mw-parser-output .cs1-hidden-error{display:none;color:var(--color-error,#bf3c2c)}.mw-parser-output .cs1-visible-error{color:var(--color-error,#bf3c2c)}.mw-parser-output .cs1-maint{display:none;color:#085;margin-left:0.3em}.mw-parser-output .cs1-kern-left{padding-left:0.2em}.mw-parser-output .cs1-kern-right{padding-right:0.2em}.mw-parser-output .citation .mw-selflink{font-weight:inherit}@media screen{.mw-parser-output .cs1-format{font-size:95%}html.skin-theme-clientpref-night .mw-parser-output .cs1-maint{color:#18911f}}@media screen and (prefers-color-scheme:dark){html.skin-theme-clientpref-os .mw-parser-output .cs1-maint{color:#18911f}}</style><cite class="citation web cs1" id="mwEnE"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20121019133659/https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Using_tab-modal_prompts" class="external text" id="mwEnI">"Mozilla Developer Network – Using tab-modal prompts"</a>. Developer.mozilla.org. 3 February 2011. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Using_tab-modal_prompts" class="external text" id="mwEnM">the original</a> on 19 October 2012<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwEnQ">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwEnU">23 May</span> 2012</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Mozilla+Developer+Network+%E2%80%93+Using+tab-modal+prompts&amp;rft.pub=Developer.mozilla.org&amp;rft.date=2011-02-03&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fdeveloper.mozilla.org%2Fen-US%2Fdocs%2FUsing_tab-modal_prompts&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AComparison+of+web+browsers" class="Z3988" id="mwEnY"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ChromePopup-146" id="cite_note-ChromePopup-146" data-mw-footnote-number="d"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEnc"><a href="#cite_ref-ChromePopup_146-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEng"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEnk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ChromePopup-146" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">The option "Do not allow any site to show pop-ups" in Google Chrome, which is the default, actually allows sites to show pop-ups which are not considered harmful.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-GoogleChromeUpdate-149" id="cite_note-GoogleChromeUpdate-149" data-mw-footnote-number="e"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEno"><a href="#cite_ref-GoogleChromeUpdate_149-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEns"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEnw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-GoogleChromeUpdate-149" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Feature was intentionally removed via regular patch update, due to poor impact on performance.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-text-modal-dialogs-153" id="cite_note-text-modal-dialogs-153" data-mw-footnote-number="f"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEn0"><a href="#cite_ref-text-modal-dialogs_153-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEn4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEn8">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-text-modal-dialogs_153-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEoA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEoE">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-text-modal-dialogs_153-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEoI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEoM">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-text-modal-dialogs-153" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Although text browsers don't have dialog windows, their prompts behave as modal dialogs – block the input until answer is received.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-QupNonBlock-154" id="cite_note-QupNonBlock-154" data-mw-footnote-number="g"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEoQ"><a href="#cite_ref-QupNonBlock_154-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEoU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEoY">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-QupNonBlock-154" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Requires building with "NONBLOCK_JS_DIALOGS" compile flag enabled; may cause crashes: <sup id="mwEoc"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwEog">[</span><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:ATODAY" title="Wikipedia:ATODAY" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEok">link removed</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwEoo">]</span></sup><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Deprecated_archive_template_links" id="mwEos"/>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Firefox_Content-modal_dialogs-156" id="cite_note-Firefox_Content-modal_dialogs-156" data-mw-footnote-number="h"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEow"><a href="#cite_ref-Firefox_Content-modal_dialogs_156-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEo0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEo4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Firefox_Content-modal_dialogs-156" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3297" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwEo8" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" id="mwEpA"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=59314" class="external text" id="mwEpE">"Bug 59314 – JavaScript alerts should be content-modal, not window-modal"</a>. Bugzilla.mozilla.org<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwEpI">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwEpM">23 May</span> 2012</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Bug+59314+%E2%80%93+JavaScript+alerts+should+be+content-modal%2C+not+window-modal&amp;rft.pub=Bugzilla.mozilla.org&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fbugzilla.mozilla.org%2Fshow_bug.cgi%3Fid%3D59314&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AComparison+of+web+browsers" class="Z3988" id="mwEpQ"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-EpiphanyAdBlock-157" id="cite_note-EpiphanyAdBlock-157" data-mw-footnote-number="i"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEpU"><a href="#cite_ref-EpiphanyAdBlock_157-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEpY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEpc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-EpiphanyAdBlock-157" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Epiphany supports <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AdBlock" title="AdBlock" id="mwEpg">AdBlock</a> as an official extension, in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epiphany-extensions" title="Epiphany-extensions" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEpk">epiphany-extensions</a> package.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IE6Tab-158" id="cite_note-IE6Tab-158" data-mw-footnote-number="j"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEpo"><a href="#cite_ref-IE6Tab_158-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEps"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEpw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IE6Tab-158" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">IE6 had no <i id="mwEp0">tabbed browsing</i> support.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IE6Popup-159" id="cite_note-IE6Popup-159" data-mw-footnote-number="k"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEp4"><a href="#cite_ref-IE6Popup_159-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEp8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEqA">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IE6Popup-159" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">IE6 included pop-up blocking with Windows XP Service Pack 2 <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.microsoft.com/WindowsXP/using/web/sp2_popupblocker.mspx" class="external autonumber" id="mwEqE"></a></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IEHistorySearch-161" id="cite_note-IEHistorySearch-161" data-mw-footnote-number="l"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEqI"><a href="#cite_ref-IEHistorySearch_161-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEqM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEqQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IEHistorySearch-161" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Full-text history search is available through a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_Search" title="Windows Search" id="mwEqU">Windows Search</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IFilter" title="IFilter" id="mwEqY">iFilter</a><sup about="#mwt2876" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-IEHisSearch_160-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"IEHisSearch"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-IEHisSearch-160"}}'><a href="#cite_note-IEHisSearch-160" id="mwEqc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwEqg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEqk">[</span>96<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEqo">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-AdBlock-162" id="cite_note-AdBlock-162" data-mw-footnote-number="m"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEqs"><a href="#cite_ref-AdBlock_162-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEqw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEq0">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-AdBlock_162-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEq4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEq8">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-AdBlock_162-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwErA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwErE">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-AdBlock_162-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwErI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwErM">4</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-AdBlock_162-4" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwErQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwErU">5</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-AdBlock_162-5" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwErY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwErc">6</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-AdBlock-162" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Most <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gecko_(layout_engine)" title="Gecko (layout engine)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwErg">Gecko</a> browsers have options to block chosen images and cookies. Extended Ad filter support can be added by installing an extension such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adblock_Plus" title="Adblock Plus" id="mwErk">Adblock Plus</a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-FilterINI-163" id="cite_note-FilterINI-163" data-mw-footnote-number="n"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEro"><a href="#cite_ref-FilterINI_163-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwErs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwErw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-FilterINI-163" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Opera 9 introduced a content blocker for webpages (<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20060209045028/http://labs.opera.com/news/2006/02/07/2/" class="external text" id="mwEr0">Archived</a> 9 February 2006 at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayback_Machine" title="Wayback Machine" id="mwEr4">Wayback Machine</a><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Webarchive_template_wayback_links" id="mwEr8"/>). Earlier releases support <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wildcard_character" title="Wildcard character" id="mwEsA">wildcard</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protocol_(computing)" title="Protocol (computing)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEsE">protocol</a>/domain/path and filetype blocking using a filter.ini file. (<link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3269" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwEsI" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" id="mwEsM"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.schrode.net/opera/url_filtering/" class="external text" id="mwEsQ">"Opera browser: Blocking unwanted ads and other cr*p using URL filtering"</a><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwEsU">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwEsY">12 April</span> 2017</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Opera+browser%3A+Blocking+unwanted+ads+and+other+cr%2Ap+using+URL+filtering&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.schrode.net%2Fopera%2Furl_filtering%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AComparison+of+web+browsers" class="Z3988" id="mwEsc"></span><span class="cs1-maint citation-comment" id="mwEsg"><code class="cs1-code" id="mwEsk">{{<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Cite_web" title="Template:Cite web" id="mwEso">cite web</a>}}</code>:  CS1 maint: deprecated archival service (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:CS1_maint:_deprecated_archival_service" title="Category:CS1 maint: deprecated archival service" id="mwEss">link</a>)</span><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:CS1_maint:_deprecated_archival_service" id="mwEsw"/>) More advanced Ad filtering for Opera can also be done with external software.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-SafariPopupBlock-164" id="cite_note-SafariPopupBlock-164" data-mw-footnote-number="o"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEs0"><a href="#cite_ref-SafariPopupBlock_164-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEs4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEs8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-SafariPopupBlock-164" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Does not allow selective blocking of pop-ups. Safari can only block all pop-ups, or none.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-SafariAdblocking-167" id="cite_note-SafariAdblocking-167" data-mw-footnote-number="p"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEtA"><a href="#cite_ref-SafariAdblocking_167-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEtE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEtI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-SafariAdblocking-167" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Ad filter support can be added by installing extensions.<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20080701200839/http://pimpmysafari.com/plugins/?c=Adblocking" class="external text" id="mwEtM">Archived</a> 1 July 2008 at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayback_Machine" title="Wayback Machine" id="mwEtQ">Wayback Machine</a><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Webarchive_template_wayback_links" id="mwEtU"/></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-iPhoneZoom-168" id="cite_note-iPhoneZoom-168" data-mw-footnote-number="q"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEtY"><a href="#cite_ref-iPhoneZoom_168-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEtc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEtg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-iPhoneZoom-168" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Page zooming supported in the iPhone version of Safari. Screen zooming is built into <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MacOS" title="MacOS" id="mwEtk">macOS</a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-onlymac-169" id="cite_note-onlymac-169" data-mw-footnote-number="r"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEto"><a href="#cite_ref-onlymac_169-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEts"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEtw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-onlymac-169" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Only Mac.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Spotlight-170" id="cite_note-Spotlight-170" data-mw-footnote-number="s"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEt0"><a href="#cite_ref-Spotlight_170-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwEt4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEt8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Spotlight-170" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Full-text history search is available through <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spotlight_(software)" title="Spotlight (software)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwEuA">Spotlight</a>, a feature of the macOS operating system.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-external-172" id="cite_note-external-172" data-mw-footnote-number="t"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwEuE"><a href="#cite_ref-external_172-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEuI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEuM">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-external_172-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEuQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEuU">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-external_172-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwEuY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwEuc">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-external-172" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">This functionality is handled by third-party software by browser's design.</span></li>
</ol></div></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwEug" aria-labelledby="Accessibility_features_(continued)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Accessibility_features_(continued)"><span id="Accessibility_features_.28continued.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Accessibility features (continued)</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Comparison_of_web_browsers&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Accessibility features (continued)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwEuk">Information about what common accessibility features are implemented natively (without third-party add-ons).
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3308" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwEuo" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sticky header","href":"./Template:Sticky_header"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1305414688" about="#mwt3309" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"template:sticky header/styles.css"}}'/></span>
