<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt3857" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwFb0" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"notelist","href":"./Template:Notelist"},"params":{"refs":{"wt":"{{efn|name=MacCaret|On macOS systems, caret navigation (called \"Full Keyboard Access\") can be enabled systemwide.}}\n{{efn|name=MacGestures|On [[Macintosh|Mac]] systems, gestures are available systemwide via multitouch sensing on trackpads and mice.}}\n{{efn|name=MacSpeech|On macOS, text-to speech and speech recognition are available systemwide and is available from menu in native Cocoa browsers.}}\n{{efn|name=ELinksSpatial|ELinks 0.12 supports spatial navigation.}}\n{{efn|name=EpiphanyGestures|Web supports mouse gestures as an extension from the [[Epiphany-extensions|official extensions package]].}}\n{{efn|name=KonqGestures|Mouse gesture support is available system-wide in [[KDE]]}}\n{{efn|name=KonqSpeech|Text-to speech support depends on the kttsd application in the kdeaccessibility package.}}\n{{efn|name=IEGestures|Mouse gesture support is available via plug-ins, i.e. [http://www.ysgyfarnog.co.uk/utilities/mousegestures/ Mouse Gestures for Internet Explorer] or [http://www.browsertools.net/Easy-Go-Back/ Easy Go Back].}}\n{{efn|name=Minimo|Doug Turner, the [[Minimo]] lead developer, has introduced spatial navigation to some special Firefox builds {{cite web |url=http://weblogs.mozillazine.org/asa/archives/007992.html |title=Adot&apos;s notblog* \"firefox, cats, mars, and more\": Spatial navigation rocks |access-date=20 April 2005 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20050422043554/http://weblogs.mozillazine.org/asa/archives/007992.html |archive-date=22 April 2005  }}. It may build as a default part of Firefox {{cite web |url=https://www.mozilla.org/access/keyboard/snav/ |title=Spatial Navigation in Mozilla |access-date=20 April 2005 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20050422001621/http://www.mozilla.org/access/keyboard/snav/ |archive-date=22 April 2005  }}.}}\n{{efn|name=MozGestures|Mouse gesture support can be added by installing extensions like All-in-One Gestures (Firefox-only) [http://marc.boullet.pagesperso-orange.fr/ext/extensions-en.html] and Mouse Gestures [http://optimoz.mozdev.org/gestures/index.html].}}\n{{efn|name=JAWS|Firefox works with a number of screen readers such as [[JAWS (screen reader)|JAWS]] and [[Microsoft Speech API]] through extensions.{{which |date=March 2012}}}}\n{{efn|name=IE8Caret|[[Internet Explorer 8]] supports caret browsing.}}\n{{efn|name=SAPITTS|[[Text-to-Speech|TTS]] in Internet Explorer and Microsoft Edge is available through the operating system [[Speech Application Programming Interface|Speech API]]. For TTS, SAPI takes text as input and uses the TTS engine to output that text as spoken audio. This is the same technology used by the Windows accessibility tool, Narrator. SAPI and an English TTS engine have been embedded in all Windows operating systems since the release of Windows XP.}}\n{{efn|name=WSR|Internet Explorer and Microsoft Edge can be controlled by applications which use the operating system [[Speech Application Programming Interface|Speech API]]. A built-in application called [[Windows Speech Recognition]] ships with [[Windows Vista]] and later client versions.}}\n{{efn|name=OperaCaret|{{Cite web |url=http://my.opera.com/shoust/blog/show.dml/305626 |title=opera : a sort of caret navigation can be enabled by a button or a shortcut |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20061101004015/http://my.opera.com/shoust/blog/show.dml/305626 |archive-date=1 November 2006 |url-status=dead |df=dmy-all }}}}\n{{efn|name=ChromeGestures|Google Chrome can be given these features using extensions like smooth gestures, speechify and voice control for google chrome.}}\n{{efn|name=QupGestures|Available as a Mouse Gestures plugin which is disabled by default, but it is part of default installation.}}\n{{efn|name=QupBookm|Supports as of v1.7.0: https://github.com/QupZilla/qupzilla/issues/458}}\n{{efn|name=QupSpatial|Available as of [https://github.com/QupZilla/qupzilla/commit/aac0956a0fedf19bab861963c570409bb2bd98dc this commit].}}\n{{efn|name=GesturesSuite|Mouse gesture support can be added by installing extensions like Mouse Gestures Suite (Seamonkey-only) [https://addons.mozilla.org/en-US/seamonkey/addon/mouse-gestures-suite/].}}\n{{efn|name=FontSmoothing|Font smoothing or [[font rasterization]] is arguably an accessibility feature affecting how the fonts are rendered and font readability. Also referred as [[ClearType]] or [[TrueType]]}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1327269900" about="#mwt3858" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Reflist/styles.css"}}'/></span><div about="#mwt3857" id="mwFb4">
<div class="mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns" typeof="mw:Extension/references" about="#mwt3907" id="mwFb8" data-mw='{"name":"references","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha","responsive":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:529}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:530}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:531}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:532}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:533}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:534}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:535}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:536}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:537}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:538}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:539}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:540}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:541}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:542}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:543}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:544}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:545}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:546}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:547}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:548}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:549}}"}}'><ol class="mw-references references" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFcA"><li about="#cite_note-FontSmoothing-173" id="cite_note-FontSmoothing-173" data-mw-footnote-number="a"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFcE"><a href="#cite_ref-FontSmoothing_173-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFcI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFcM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-FontSmoothing-173" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Font smoothing or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Font_rasterization" title="Font rasterization" id="mwFcQ">font rasterization</a> is arguably an accessibility feature affecting how the fonts are rendered and font readability. Also referred as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ClearType" title="ClearType" id="mwFcU">ClearType</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TrueType" title="TrueType" id="mwFcY">TrueType</a></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-MacGestures-174" id="cite_note-MacGestures-174" data-mw-footnote-number="b"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFcc"><a href="#cite_ref-MacGestures_174-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFcg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFck">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MacGestures_174-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFco"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFcs">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MacGestures_174-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFcw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFc0">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-MacGestures-174" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">On <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macintosh" title="Macintosh" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFc4">Mac</a> systems, gestures are available systemwide via multitouch sensing on trackpads and mice.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-MacSpeech-175" id="cite_note-MacSpeech-175" data-mw-footnote-number="c"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFc8"><a href="#cite_ref-MacSpeech_175-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFdA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFdE">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MacSpeech_175-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFdI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFdM">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MacSpeech_175-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFdQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFdU">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MacSpeech_175-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFdY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFdc">4</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-MacSpeech-175" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">On macOS, text-to speech and speech recognition are available systemwide and is available from menu in native Cocoa browsers.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ChromeGestures-176" id="cite_note-ChromeGestures-176" data-mw-footnote-number="d"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFdg"><a href="#cite_ref-ChromeGestures_176-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFdk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFdo">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ChromeGestures_176-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFds"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFdw">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ChromeGestures_176-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFd0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFd4">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ChromeGestures_176-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFd8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFeA">4</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ChromeGestures_176-4" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFeE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFeI">5</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ChromeGestures_176-5" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFeM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFeQ">6</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ChromeGestures-176" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Google Chrome can be given these features using extensions like smooth gestures, speechify and voice control for google chrome.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-SAPITTS-177" id="cite_note-SAPITTS-177" data-mw-footnote-number="e"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFeU"><a href="#cite_ref-SAPITTS_177-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFeY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFec">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-SAPITTS_177-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFeg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFek">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-SAPITTS-177" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Text-to-Speech" title="Text-to-Speech" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFeo">TTS</a> in Internet Explorer and Microsoft Edge is available through the operating system <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speech_Application_Programming_Interface" title="Speech Application Programming Interface" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFes">Speech API</a>. For TTS, SAPI takes text as input and uses the TTS engine to output that text as spoken audio. This is the same technology used by the Windows accessibility tool, Narrator. SAPI and an English TTS engine have been embedded in all Windows operating systems since the release of Windows XP.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-WSR-178" id="cite_note-WSR-178" data-mw-footnote-number="f"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFew"><a href="#cite_ref-WSR_178-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFe0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFe4">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-WSR_178-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFe8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFfA">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-WSR-178" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Internet Explorer and Microsoft Edge can be controlled by applications which use the operating system <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speech_Application_Programming_Interface" title="Speech Application Programming Interface" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFfE">Speech API</a>. A built-in application called <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_Speech_Recognition" title="Windows Speech Recognition" id="mwFfI">Windows Speech Recognition</a> ships with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows_Vista" title="Windows Vista" id="mwFfM">Windows Vista</a> and later client versions.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ELinksSpatial-179" id="cite_note-ELinksSpatial-179" data-mw-footnote-number="g"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFfQ"><a href="#cite_ref-ELinksSpatial_179-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFfU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFfY">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ELinksSpatial-179" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">ELinks 0.12 supports spatial navigation.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-QupSpatial-180" id="cite_note-QupSpatial-180" data-mw-footnote-number="h"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFfc"><a href="#cite_ref-QupSpatial_180-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFfg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFfk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-QupSpatial-180" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Available as of <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://github.com/QupZilla/qupzilla/commit/aac0956a0fedf19bab861963c570409bb2bd98dc" class="external text" id="mwFfo">this commit</a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-QupBookm-181" id="cite_note-QupBookm-181" data-mw-footnote-number="i"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFfs"><a href="#cite_ref-QupBookm_181-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFfw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFf0">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-QupBookm-181" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Supports as of v1.7.0: <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://github.com/QupZilla/qupzilla/issues/458" class="external free" id="mwFf4">https://github.com/QupZilla/qupzilla/issues/458</a></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-QupGestures-182" id="cite_note-QupGestures-182" data-mw-footnote-number="j"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFf8"><a href="#cite_ref-QupGestures_182-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFgA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFgE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-QupGestures-182" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Available as a Mouse Gestures plugin which is disabled by default, but it is part of default installation.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-Minimo-183" id="cite_note-Minimo-183" data-mw-footnote-number="k"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFgI"><a href="#cite_ref-Minimo_183-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFgM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFgQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Minimo-183" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Doug Turner, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minimo" title="Minimo" id="mwFgU">Minimo</a> lead developer, has introduced spatial navigation to some special Firefox builds <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3875" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwFgY" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" id="mwFgc"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20050422043554/http://weblogs.mozillazine.org/asa/archives/007992.html" class="external text" id="mwFgg">"Adot's notblog* "firefox, cats, mars, and more": Spatial navigation rocks"</a>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://weblogs.mozillazine.org/asa/archives/007992.html" class="external text" id="mwFgk">the original</a> on 22 April 2005<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwFgo">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwFgs">20 April</span> 2005</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Adot%27s+notblog%2A+%22firefox%2C+cats%2C+mars%2C+and+more%22%3A+Spatial+navigation+rocks&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fweblogs.mozillazine.org%2Fasa%2Farchives%2F007992.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AComparison+of+web+browsers" class="Z3988" id="mwFgw"></span>. It may build as a default part of Firefox <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3876" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwFg0" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" id="mwFg4"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20050422001621/http://www.mozilla.org/access/keyboard/snav/" class="external text" id="mwFg8">"Spatial Navigation in Mozilla"</a>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.mozilla.org/access/keyboard/snav/" class="external text" id="mwFhA">the original</a> on 22 April 2005<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwFhE">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwFhI">20 April</span> 2005</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Spatial+Navigation+in+Mozilla&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.mozilla.org%2Faccess%2Fkeyboard%2Fsnav%2F&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AComparison+of+web+browsers" class="Z3988" id="mwFhM"></span>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-MozGestures-184" id="cite_note-MozGestures-184" data-mw-footnote-number="l"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFhQ"><a href="#cite_ref-MozGestures_184-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFhU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFhY">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozGestures_184-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFhc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFhg">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-MozGestures-184" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Mouse gesture support can be added by installing extensions like All-in-One Gestures (Firefox-only) <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://marc.boullet.pagesperso-orange.fr/ext/extensions-en.html" class="external autonumber" id="mwFhk"></a> and Mouse Gestures <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://optimoz.mozdev.org/gestures/index.html" class="external autonumber" id="mwFho"></a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-JAWS-185" id="cite_note-JAWS-185" data-mw-footnote-number="m"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFhs"><a href="#cite_ref-JAWS_185-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFhw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFh0">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-JAWS-185" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Firefox works with a number of screen readers such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JAWS_(screen_reader)" title="JAWS (screen reader)" id="mwFh4">JAWS</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Speech_API" title="Microsoft Speech API" id="mwFh8">Microsoft Speech API</a> through extensions.<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_specifically_marked_weasel-worded_phrases" id="mwFiA"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_specifically_marked_weasel-worded_phrases_from_March_2012" id="mwFiE"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template " style="white-space:nowrap;" id="mwFiI"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwFiM">[</span><i id="mwFiQ"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Avoid_weasel_words" title="Wikipedia:Avoid weasel words" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFiU"><span title="The material near this tag possibly uses too vague attribution or weasel words. (March 2012)" id="mwFiY">which?</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwFic">]</span></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IE8Caret-186" id="cite_note-IE8Caret-186" data-mw-footnote-number="n"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFig"><a href="#cite_ref-IE8Caret_186-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFik"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFio">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IE8Caret-186" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Explorer_8" title="Internet Explorer 8" id="mwFis">Internet Explorer 8</a> supports caret browsing.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IEGestures-187" id="cite_note-IEGestures-187" data-mw-footnote-number="o"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFiw"><a href="#cite_ref-IEGestures_187-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFi0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFi4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IEGestures-187" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Mouse gesture support is available via plug-ins, i.e. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.ysgyfarnog.co.uk/utilities/mousegestures/" class="external text" id="mwFi8">Mouse Gestures for Internet Explorer</a> or <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.browsertools.net/Easy-Go-Back/" class="external text" id="mwFjA">Easy Go Back</a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-KonqGestures-188" id="cite_note-KonqGestures-188" data-mw-footnote-number="p"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFjE"><a href="#cite_ref-KonqGestures_188-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFjI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFjM">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-KonqGestures-188" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Mouse gesture support is available system-wide in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KDE" title="KDE" id="mwFjQ">KDE</a></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-KonqSpeech-189" id="cite_note-KonqSpeech-189" data-mw-footnote-number="q"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFjU"><a href="#cite_ref-KonqSpeech_189-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFjY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFjc">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-KonqSpeech-189" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Text-to speech support depends on the kttsd application in the kdeaccessibility package.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-OperaCaret-190" id="cite_note-OperaCaret-190" data-mw-footnote-number="r"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFjg"><a href="#cite_ref-OperaCaret_190-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFjk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFjo">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-OperaCaret-190" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt3891" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwFjs" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" id="mwFjw"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20061101004015/http://my.opera.com/shoust/blog/show.dml/305626" class="external text" id="mwFj0">"opera<span typeof="mw:DisplaySpace" id="mwFj4"> </span>: a sort of caret navigation can be enabled by a button or a shortcut"</a>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://my.opera.com/shoust/blog/show.dml/305626" class="external text" id="mwFj8">the original</a> on 1 November 2006.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=opera+%3A+a+sort+of+caret+navigation+can+be+enabled+by+a+button+or+a+shortcut&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fmy.opera.com%2Fshoust%2Fblog%2Fshow.dml%2F305626&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AComparison+of+web+browsers" class="Z3988" id="mwFkA"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-onlymac-191" id="cite_note-onlymac-191" data-mw-footnote-number="s"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFkE"><a href="#cite_ref-onlymac_191-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFkI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFkM">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-onlymac_191-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFkQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFkU">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-onlymac_191-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFkY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFkc">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-onlymac_191-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwFkg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFkk">4</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-onlymac-191" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Only Mac.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-MacCaret-192" id="cite_note-MacCaret-192" data-mw-footnote-number="t"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFko"><a href="#cite_ref-MacCaret_192-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFks"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFkw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-MacCaret-192" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">On macOS systems, caret navigation (called "Full Keyboard Access") can be enabled systemwide.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-GesturesSuite-193" id="cite_note-GesturesSuite-193" data-mw-footnote-number="u"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFk0"><a href="#cite_ref-GesturesSuite_193-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwFk4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwFk8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-GesturesSuite-193" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Mouse gesture support can be added by installing extensions like Mouse Gestures Suite (Seamonkey-only) <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://addons.mozilla.org/en-US/seamonkey/addon/mouse-gestures-suite/" class="external autonumber" id="mwFlA"></a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-EpiphanyGestures-194" id="cite_note-EpiphanyGestures-194" data-mw-footnote-number="v"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwFlE"></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-EpiphanyGestures-194" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Web supports mouse gestures as an extension from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epiphany-extensions" title="Epiphany-extensions" class="mw-redirect" id="mwFlI">official extensions package</a>.</span></li>
</ol><span typeof="mw:I18n" class="error mw-ext-cite-error" id="mwFlM" lang="en" dir="ltr" data-mw-i18n='{"/":{"lang":"x-user","key":"cite_error","params":[{"text":{"key":"cite_error_references_missing_key","params":["EpiphanyGestures"]}}]}}'>Cite error: A <a href="/wiki/Help:Footnotes#WP:LDR" title="Help:Footnotes">list-defined reference</a> named "EpiphanyGestures" is not used in the content (see the <a href="/wiki/Help:Cite_errors/Cite_error_references_missing_key" title="Help:Cite errors/Cite error references missing key">help page</a>).</span></div></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwFlQ" aria-labelledby="Web_technology_support"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Web_technology_support">Web technology support</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Comparison_of_web_browsers&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: Web technology support"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwFlU">Information about what web standards, and technologies the browsers support, except for JavaScript. External links lead to information about support in future versions of the browsers or extensions that provide such functionality.
