</tbody></table>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt4453" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwGNE" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"notelist","href":"./Template:Notelist"},"params":{"refs":{"wt":"{{efn|name=CSS2|CSS 2, a [[World Wide Web Consortium|W3C]] recommendation since 1998, is the current stable version of CSS, nevertheless, CSS 2.1 corrects a few errors in CSS2 (the most important being a new definition of the height/width of absolutely positioned elements, more influence for HTML&apos;s \"style\" attribute and a new calculation of the &apos;clip&apos; property), and adds a few highly requested features which have already been widely implemented. CSS 2.1 is derived from and is intended to replace CSS 2. Conformance criteria are detailed [http://www.w3.org/TR/CSS21/conform.html at the W3C website].&lt;!-- Are we following those criteria or not? We certainly should be. --> (CSS 3 is only in draft status at present.) For more detailed information please see [[comparison of layout engines (CSS)]].}}\n{{efn|name=frames|Frames and frame sets are [http://www.w3.org/TR/html5/obsolete.html#non-conforming-features obsolete and non-conforming in HTML5]. They should not be used by authors.}}\n{{efn|name=LINK|LINK as a navigational aid, as distinct from non-navigational uses of LINK.}}\n{{efn|name=LINKext|Not in standard install, but provided by extension.[http://www.christophm.de/software/firefox/cmSiteNavigation/] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080714034115/http://www.christophm.de/software/firefox/cmSiteNavigation/ |date=14 July 2008 }} [http://webcoder.info/reference/LinkBars.html] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080513152357/http://webcoder.info/reference/LinkBars.html |date=13 May 2008 }}}}\n{{efn|name=XHTML|[[XHTML]] is based on [[HTML]] but is an application of XML, which means that XHTML must be stricter than equivalent HTML code. XHTML is meant to be read by an XML parser but for [[backward compatibility]] reasons can also be parsed as HTML; this table only notes the browsers that are able to parse XHTML as XML. For more detailed information please see comparison of layout engines (XHTML).}}\n{{efn|name=DilloFrames|[[Dillo]] displays frames as links that the user can click on.}}\n{{efn|name=IEMathML|Available with the MathPlayer plugin.}}\n&lt;!--IE8CSS2 defined above because of nested ref tags-->\n{{efn|name=luna|Depends on the [[Browser engine|layout engine]] which is chosen: Trident or Gecko or WebKit.}}\n{{efn|name=ns8|Depends on the [[Browser engine|layout engine]] which is chosen: Trident or Gecko.}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1327269900" about="#mwt4454" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Reflist/styles.css"}}'/></span><div about="#mwt4453" id="mwGNI">
<div class="mw-references-wrap" typeof="mw:Extension/references" about="#mwt4473" id="mwGNM" data-mw='{"name":"references","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha","responsive":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:602}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:603}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:604}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:605}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:606}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:607}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:608}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:609}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:610}}"}}'><ol class="mw-references references" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGNQ"><li about="#cite_note-CSS2-195" id="cite_note-CSS2-195" data-mw-footnote-number="a"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGNU"><a href="#cite_ref-CSS2_195-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGNY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGNc">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-CSS2_195-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGNg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGNk">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-CSS2-195" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">CSS 2, a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Wide_Web_Consortium" title="World Wide Web Consortium" id="mwGNo">W3C</a> recommendation since 1998, is the current stable version of CSS, nevertheless, CSS 2.1 corrects a few errors in CSS2 (the most important being a new definition of the height/width of absolutely positioned elements, more influence for HTML's "style" attribute and a new calculation of the 'clip' property), and adds a few highly requested features which have already been widely implemented. CSS 2.1 is derived from and is intended to replace CSS 2. Conformance criteria are detailed <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.w3.org/TR/CSS21/conform.html" class="external text" id="mwGNs">at the W3C website</a>. (CSS 3 is only in draft status at present.) For more detailed information please see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comparison_of_layout_engines_(CSS)?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="Comparison of layout engines (CSS) (page does not exist)" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" id="mwGNw" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["Comparison of layout engines (CSS)"]}}'>comparison of layout engines (CSS)</a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-frames-196" id="cite_note-frames-196" data-mw-footnote-number="b"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGN0"><a href="#cite_ref-frames_196-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGN4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGN8">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-frames_196-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGOA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGOE">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-frames-196" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Frames and frame sets are <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.w3.org/TR/html5/obsolete.html#non-conforming-features" class="external text" id="mwGOI">obsolete and non-conforming in HTML5</a>. They should not be used by authors.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-LINK-197" id="cite_note-LINK-197" data-mw-footnote-number="c"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGOM"><a href="#cite_ref-LINK_197-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGOQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGOU">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-LINK_197-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGOY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGOc">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-LINK-197" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">LINK as a navigational aid, as distinct from non-navigational uses of LINK.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-XHTML-198" id="cite_note-XHTML-198" data-mw-footnote-number="d"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGOg"><a href="#cite_ref-XHTML_198-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGOk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGOo">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-XHTML_198-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGOs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGOw">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-XHTML-198" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/XHTML" title="XHTML" id="mwGO0">XHTML</a> is based on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML" title="HTML" id="mwGO4">HTML</a> but is an application of XML, which means that XHTML must be stricter than equivalent HTML code. XHTML is meant to be read by an XML parser but for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backward_compatibility" title="Backward compatibility" id="mwGO8">backward compatibility</a> reasons can also be parsed as HTML; this table only notes the browsers that are able to parse XHTML as XML. For more detailed information please see comparison of layout engines (XHTML).</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IEMathML-199" id="cite_note-IEMathML-199" data-mw-footnote-number="e"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGPA"><a href="#cite_ref-IEMathML_199-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGPE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGPI">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-IEMathML_199-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGPM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGPQ">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-IEMathML_199-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGPU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGPY">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IEMathML-199" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Available with the MathPlayer plugin.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-DilloFrames-200" id="cite_note-DilloFrames-200" data-mw-footnote-number="f"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGPc"><a href="#cite_ref-DilloFrames_200-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwGPg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGPk">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-DilloFrames-200" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dillo" title="Dillo" id="mwGPo">Dillo</a> displays frames as links that the user can click on.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-LINKext-201" id="cite_note-LINKext-201" data-mw-footnote-number="g"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGPs"><a href="#cite_ref-LINKext_201-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGPw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGP0">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-LINKext_201-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGP4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGP8">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-LINKext_201-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGQA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGQE">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-LINKext_201-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGQI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGQM">4</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-LINKext-201" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Not in standard install, but provided by extension.<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.christophm.de/software/firefox/cmSiteNavigation/" class="external autonumber" id="mwGQQ"></a> <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20080714034115/http://www.christophm.de/software/firefox/cmSiteNavigation/" class="external text" id="mwGQU">Archived</a> 14 July 2008 at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayback_Machine" title="Wayback Machine" id="mwGQY">Wayback Machine</a><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Webarchive_template_wayback_links" id="mwGQc"/> <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://webcoder.info/reference/LinkBars.html" class="external autonumber" id="mwGQg"></a> <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20080513152357/http://webcoder.info/reference/LinkBars.html" class="external text" id="mwGQk">Archived</a> 13 May 2008 at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayback_Machine" title="Wayback Machine" id="mwGQo">Wayback Machine</a><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Webarchive_template_wayback_links" id="mwGQs"/></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IE8CSS2-204" id="cite_note-IE8CSS2-204" data-mw-footnote-number="h"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGQw"><a href="#cite_ref-IE8CSS2_204-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwGQ0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGQ4">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IE8CSS2-204" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Microsoft claims Internet Explorer 8 has full CSS2.1 support,<sup about="#mwt4118" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-IE8CSS2-ref_202-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"IE8CSS2-ref"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-IE8CSS2-ref-202"}}'><a href="#cite_note-IE8CSS2-ref-202" id="mwGQ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGRA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGRE">[</span>100<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGRI">]</span></span></a></sup> however independent testing revealed several bugs.<sup about="#mwt4123" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-IE8CSS2Bugs_203-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"IE8CSS2Bugs"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-IE8CSS2Bugs-203"}}'><a href="#cite_note-IE8CSS2Bugs-203" id="mwGRM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGRQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGRU">[</span>101<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGRY">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-luna-205" id="cite_note-luna-205" data-mw-footnote-number="i"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGRc"><a href="#cite_ref-luna_205-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGRg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGRk">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-luna_205-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGRo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGRs">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-luna_205-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGRw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGR0">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-luna-205" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Depends on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Browser_engine" title="Browser engine" id="mwGR4">layout engine</a> which is chosen: Trident or Gecko or WebKit.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ns8-206" id="cite_note-ns8-206" data-mw-footnote-number="j"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwGR8"><a href="#cite_ref-ns8_206-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGSA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGSE">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ns8_206-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGSI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGSM">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ns8_206-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGSQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwGSU">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ns8-206" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Depends on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Browser_engine" title="Browser engine" id="mwGSY">layout engine</a> which is chosen: Trident or Gecko.</span></li>
</ol></div></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwGSc" aria-labelledby="Plugins_and_syndicated_content_support"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Plugins_and_syndicated_content_support">Plugins and syndicated content support</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Comparison_of_web_browsers&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Plugins and syndicated content support"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwGSg">Information about what web standards, and technologies the browsers support. External links lead to information about support in future versions of the browsers or extensions that provide such functionality.
