<th style="background: #F4E3FF; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: left; font-weight: bolder; " scope="row" class="rh heading table-rh" about="#mwt4661" typeof="mw:ExpandedAttrs" id="mwGg8" data-mw='{"attribs":[[{"txt":"style","html":"&lt;span about=\"#mwt4660\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwGg4\" data-mw=&apos;{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"rh2\",\"href\":\"./Template:Rh2\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}&apos;>style=\"background: &lt;/span>&lt;span typeof=\"mw:Nowiki\" about=\"#mwt4660\">#F4E3FF&lt;/span>&lt;span about=\"#mwt4660\">; color: black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: left; font-weight: bolder; \" scope=\"row\" class=\"rh heading table-rh\"&lt;/span>"},{"html":""}]]}'><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Explorer" title="Internet Explorer" id="mwGhA">Internet Explorer</a></th>
<td style="background:#9EFF9E;color:black;vertical-align:middle;text-align:center;" class="table-yes skin-invert" typeof="mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt4662" id="mwGhE" data-mw='{"parts":["| ",{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Yes","href":"./Template:Yes"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'>Yes</td>
<td style="background: #FED; color:black; vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; " class="dropped table-dropped" typeof="mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt4663" id="mwGhI" data-mw='{"parts":["| ",{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Dropped","href":"./Template:Dropped"},"params":{},"i":0}},"{{efn|name=IENPAPI|Internet Explorer did for a time support NPAPI plugins. Plugins that functioned in the Netscape browser also functioned in Internet Explorer. This was due to a small ActiveX control implemented within a \"plugin.ocx\" file that acted as a shim between the ActiveX based browser and the NPAPI plugin. The IE browser would load the control and use it to host plugins specified within the page. However, Microsoft made the claim that the NPAPI plugins (or the IE implementation of the API) were a security issue and dropped support for them in version [[Internet Explorer 5|5.5 SP2]].&lt;ref>{{cite web|url=http://support.microsoft.com/kb/303401|title=Netscape-style plug-ins do not work after upgrading Internet Explorer|date=21 May 2004|publisher=[[Microsoft]]|access-date=17 May 2009}}&lt;/ref>&lt;ref>{{cite web|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071016233843/http://www.meer.net/jg/broken-plugins.html|archive-date=16 October 2007|url=http://www.meer.net/jg/broken-plugins.html|title=Microsoft breaks Web Plugins in Windows XP|last=Giannandrea|first=J.|date=4 September 2001|access-date=17 May 2009}}&lt;/ref>&lt;ref>{{cite web|url=http://support.microsoft.com/kb/306790|title=Description of Internet Explorer Support for Netscape-Style Plug-ins|date=31 January 2007|publisher=[[Microsoft]]|access-date=17 May 2009}}&lt;/ref>}}"]}'>Dropped<sup about="#mwt4664" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-IENPAPI_217-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"IENPAPI","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-IENPAPI-217"},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"IENPAPI"},"1":{"wt":"Internet Explorer did for a time support NPAPI plugins. Plugins that functioned in the Netscape browser also functioned in Internet Explorer. This was due to a small ActiveX control implemented within a \"plugin.ocx\" file that acted as a shim between the ActiveX based browser and the NPAPI plugin. The IE browser would load the control and use it to host plugins specified within the page. However, Microsoft made the claim that the NPAPI plugins (or the IE implementation of the API) were a security issue and dropped support for them in version [[Internet Explorer 5|5.5 SP2]].&lt;ref>{{cite web|url=http://support.microsoft.com/kb/303401|title=Netscape-style plug-ins do not work after upgrading Internet Explorer|date=21 May 2004|publisher=[[Microsoft]]|access-date=17 May 2009}}&lt;/ref>&lt;ref>{{cite web|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071016233843/http://www.meer.net/jg/broken-plugins.html|archive-date=16 October 2007|url=http://www.meer.net/jg/broken-plugins.html|title=Microsoft breaks Web Plugins in Windows XP|last=Giannandrea|first=J.|date=4 September 2001|access-date=17 May 2009}}&lt;/ref>&lt;ref>{{cite web|url=http://support.microsoft.com/kb/306790|title=Description of Internet Explorer Support for Netscape-Style Plug-ins|date=31 January 2007|publisher=[[Microsoft]]|access-date=17 May 2009}}&lt;/ref>"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-IENPAPI-217" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwGhM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGhQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGhU">[</span>f<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGhY">]</span></span></a></sup></td>
