<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt5531" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwHkw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"notelist","href":"./Template:Notelist"},"params":{"refs":{"wt":"{{efn|name=IEDOM2|Internet Explorer 5 and above has [http://www.quirksmode.org/js/events_advanced.html its own event registration model] and [http://www.quirksmode.org/dom/changess.html its own style sheets model], but these are incompatible with DOM 2.}}\n{{efn|name=MozXPath|XPath is a part of DOM 3, but is considered separately here. A large subset of DOM 3 is accessible by extensions but not by websites.}}\n{{efn|name=SafariNightly|SVG, XPath, (partial) DOM 3 is available in only the WebKit nightlies so far.}}\n{{efn|name=AmayaScript|It is possible to compile [https://web.archive.org/web/20071225120656/http://www.maths-informatique-jeux.com/international/javascript_in_amaya/ Amaya with JavaScript enabled], using the CVS version and [[SpiderMonkey]]. However, this is still experimental and only a small subset of DOM 1 is available.}}\n{{efn|name=LinksScript|Support for JavaScript has been removed in version 2.1pre29 ([http://links.twibright.com/download/ChangeLog change log])}}\n{{efn|name=ns8|Depends on the [[Browser engine|layout engine]] which is chosen: Trident or Gecko.}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1327269900" about="#mwt5532" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Reflist/styles.css"}}'/></span><div about="#mwt5531" id="mwHk0">
<div class="mw-references-wrap" typeof="mw:Extension/references" about="#mwt5545" id="mwHk4" data-mw='{"name":"references","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha","responsive":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:718}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:719}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:720}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:721}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:722}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:723}}"}}'><ol class="mw-references references" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHk8"><li about="#cite_note-AmayaScript-223" id="cite_note-AmayaScript-223" data-mw-footnote-number="a"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwHlA"><a href="#cite_ref-AmayaScript_223-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHlE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHlI">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-AmayaScript_223-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHlM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHlQ">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-AmayaScript_223-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHlU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHlY">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-AmayaScript-223" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">It is possible to compile <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20071225120656/http://www.maths-informatique-jeux.com/international/javascript_in_amaya/" class="external text" id="mwHlc">Amaya with JavaScript enabled</a>, using the CVS version and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SpiderMonkey" title="SpiderMonkey" id="mwHlg">SpiderMonkey</a>. However, this is still experimental and only a small subset of DOM 1 is available.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-MozXPath-224" id="cite_note-MozXPath-224" data-mw-footnote-number="b"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwHlk"><a href="#cite_ref-MozXPath_224-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHlo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHls">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozXPath_224-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHlw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHl0">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozXPath_224-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHl4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHl8">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozXPath_224-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHmA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHmE">4</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozXPath_224-4" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHmI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHmM">5</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozXPath_224-5" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHmQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHmU">6</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozXPath_224-6" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHmY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHmc">7</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozXPath_224-7" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHmg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHmk">8</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozXPath_224-8" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHmo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHms">9</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozXPath_224-9" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHmw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHm0">10</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozXPath_224-10" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHm4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHm8">11</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozXPath_224-11" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHnA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHnE">12</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-MozXPath-224" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">XPath is a part of DOM 3, but is considered separately here. A large subset of DOM 3 is accessible by extensions but not by websites.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-225" id="cite_note-225" data-mw-footnote-number="c"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwHnI"><a href="#cite_ref-225" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwHnM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHnQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-225" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Determined by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU_LibreJS" title="GNU LibreJS" id="mwHnU">GNU LibreJS</a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IEDOM2-226" id="cite_note-IEDOM2-226" data-mw-footnote-number="d"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwHnY"><a href="#cite_ref-IEDOM2_226-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHnc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHng">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-IEDOM2_226-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHnk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHno">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IEDOM2-226" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Internet Explorer 5 and above has <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.quirksmode.org/js/events_advanced.html" class="external text" id="mwHns">its own event registration model</a> and <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.quirksmode.org/dom/changess.html" class="external text" id="mwHnw">its own style sheets model</a>, but these are incompatible with DOM 2.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-LinksScript-227" id="cite_note-LinksScript-227" data-mw-footnote-number="e"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwHn0"><a href="#cite_ref-LinksScript_227-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwHn4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHn8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-LinksScript-227" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Support for JavaScript has been removed in version 2.1pre29 (<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://links.twibright.com/download/ChangeLog" class="external text" id="mwHoA">change log</a>)</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-SafariNightly-228" id="cite_note-SafariNightly-228" data-mw-footnote-number="f"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwHoE"><a href="#cite_ref-SafariNightly_228-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHoI"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHoM">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-SafariNightly_228-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHoQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHoU">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-SafariNightly_228-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHoY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHoc">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-SafariNightly_228-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHog"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHok">4</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-SafariNightly_228-4" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHoo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHos">5</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-SafariNightly-228" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">SVG, XPath, (partial) DOM 3 is available in only the WebKit nightlies so far.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ns8-229" id="cite_note-ns8-229" data-mw-footnote-number="g"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwHow"><a href="#cite_ref-ns8_229-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHo0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHo4">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ns8_229-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHo8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHpA">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ns8_229-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHpE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwHpI">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ns8-229" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Depends on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Browser_engine" title="Browser engine" id="mwHpM">layout engine</a> which is chosen: Trident or Gecko.</span></li>
</ol></div></div>

<p id="mwHpQ"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.howtocreate.co.uk/tutorials/jsexamples/hasFeature.html" class="external text" id="mwHpU">See what parts of DOM your browser supports</a></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwHpY" aria-labelledby="Protocol_support"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Protocol_support">Protocol support</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Comparison_of_web_browsers&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section: Protocol support"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwHpc">Information about what <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_protocols" title="Internet protocols" class="mw-redirect" id="mwHpg">Internet protocols</a> the browsers support (in addition to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP" title="HTTP" id="mwHpk">HTTP</a> that all (modern) browser should and do fully support<sup about="#mwt5546" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Mosaic_230-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Mosaic","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"html":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"Mosaic"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-Mosaic-230" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwHpo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHps"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHpw">[</span>a<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHp0">]</span></span></a></sup>). External links lead to information about support in future versions of the browsers or extensions that provide such functionality.</p>

<p id="mwHp4">More than half of web traffic from Chrome to Google's servers is handled by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/QUIC" title="QUIC" id="mwHp8">QUIC</a> protocol, not <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transmission_Control_Protocol" title="Transmission Control Protocol" id="mwHqA">TCP</a> (or HTTP/1). Chrome, Opera, and Firefox have support for QUIC, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP/3" title="HTTP/3" id="mwHqE">HTTP/3</a>, while Safari is testing it for a subset of users.
<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt5549" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwHqI" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"sticky header","href":"./Template:Sticky_header"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1305414688" about="#mwt5550" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"template:sticky header/styles.css"}}'/></span></p>
