</tbody></table>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt6373" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwIk4" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"notelist","href":"./Template:Notelist"},"params":{"refs":{"wt":"{{efn|name=External2|Many browsers have FTP support as read-only and have no upload capitilies. Read-only is marked as yes. For a comparison of clients that support upload opportunities see Comparison of FTP client software.}}\n{{efn|name=External3|Many browsers have purposely avoided support for e-mail and newsgroups ([[Usenet]]), as these are reserved for their mail-client counterparts. For a comparison of such counterparts see [[comparison of email clients]] and [[Comparison of Usenet newsreaders]].}}\n&lt;!--IE is declared above because of nested tags-->\n{{efn|name=Mosaic|Mosaic reached only HTTP 0.9 compliance, and does not support secure communications in any way.}}\n{{efn|name=ChatZilla|IRC support can be added by installing [[ChatZilla]].}}\n&lt;!--FirefoxGopherDropped is declared above because of nested tags-->\n{{efn|name=OpGopher|Includes a proxy capability for gopher support.}}\n{{efn|name=IEGopher|Internet Explorer 7 has no support of gopher; gopher support is disabled in IE6.}}\n{{efn|name=MozIDN|For security reasons, IDN domains are displayed as [[punycode]] if they contain certain characters or if the [[top-level domain]] has not been [[whitelist]]ed [http://kb.mozillazine.org/Network.IDN.blacklist_chars].}}\n{{efn|name=KonqGopher|Konqueror has full Gopher support when the kgopher KIO plugin is installed.}}\n{{efn|name=NNTP|[[NNTP]] support can be added by installing the add-on [[infoRSS]].}}\n{{efn|name=DilloSSL|Dillo has experimental SSL integration that is by standard turned off. {{cite web |url=http://www.dillo.org/FAQ.html#q12 |title=How do I enable the https (SSL) support plugin for dillo? |access-date=12 April 2017 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080509062517/http://www.dillo.org/FAQ.html#q12 |archive-date=9 May 2008 |url-status=dead }} There is no certificate caching and &apos;&apos;no authentication&apos;&apos; performed.}}\n&lt;!--firetorrent is declared above because of nested tags-->\n{{efn|name=no-ui|Behavior towards malicious certificates can only be set up in [[compiler|compile time]].}}\n&lt;!--IEdataprotocol is declared above because of nested ref tags-->\n{{efn|name=system-wide|Respects system-wide proxy settings.}}\n{{efn|name=ns8|Depends on the [[Browser engine|layout engine]] which is chosen: Trident or Gecko.}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1327269900" about="#mwt6374" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Reflist/styles.css"}}'/></span><div about="#mwt6373" id="mwIk8">
<div class="mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns" typeof="mw:Extension/references" about="#mwt6403" id="mwIlA" data-mw='{"name":"references","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha","responsive":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:805}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:806}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:807}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:808}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:809}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:810}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:811}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:812}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:813}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:814}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:815}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:816}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:817}}"}}'><ol class="mw-references references" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIlE"><li about="#cite_note-Mosaic-230" id="cite_note-Mosaic-230" data-mw-footnote-number="a"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIlI"><a href="#cite_ref-Mosaic_230-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIlM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIlQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-Mosaic-230" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Mosaic reached only HTTP 0.9 compliance, and does not support secure communications in any way.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-External2-231" id="cite_note-External2-231" data-mw-footnote-number="b"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIlU"><a href="#cite_ref-External2_231-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIlY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIlc">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-External2_231-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIlg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIlk">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-External2-231" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Many browsers have FTP support as read-only and have no upload capitilies. Read-only is marked as yes. For a comparison of clients that support upload opportunities see Comparison of FTP client software.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-External3-232" id="cite_note-External3-232" data-mw-footnote-number="c"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIlo"><a href="#cite_ref-External3_232-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIls"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIlw">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-External3_232-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIl0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIl4">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-External3-232" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Many browsers have purposely avoided support for e-mail and newsgroups (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Usenet" title="Usenet" id="mwIl8">Usenet</a>), as these are reserved for their mail-client counterparts. For a comparison of such counterparts see <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comparison_of_email_clients" title="Comparison of email clients" id="mwImA">comparison of email clients</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comparison_of_Usenet_newsreaders" title="Comparison of Usenet newsreaders" class="mw-redirect" id="mwImE">Comparison of Usenet newsreaders</a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IE-233" id="cite_note-IE-233" data-mw-footnote-number="d"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwImI"><a href="#cite_ref-IE_233-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwImM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwImQ">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-IE_233-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwImU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwImY">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-IE_233-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwImc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwImg">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-IE_233-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwImk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwImo">4</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IE-233" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Support for 256-bit ciphers (AES for example) for SSL/TLS is only available in Windows Vista and above<sup about="#mwt5875" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-247" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-247"}}'><a href="#cite_note-247" id="mwIms"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwImw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIm0">[</span>113<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIm4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt5880" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-248" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-248"}}'><a href="#cite_note-248" id="mwIm8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwInA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwInE">[</span>114<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwInI">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IEGopher-234" id="cite_note-IEGopher-234" data-mw-footnote-number="e"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwInM"><a href="#cite_ref-IEGopher_234-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwInQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwInU">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-IEGopher_234-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwInY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwInc">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-IEGopher_234-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIng"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwInk">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-IEGopher_234-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIno"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIns">4</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IEGopher-234" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Internet Explorer 7 has no support of gopher; gopher support is disabled in IE6.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-NNTP-235" id="cite_note-NNTP-235" data-mw-footnote-number="f"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwInw"><a href="#cite_ref-NNTP_235-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIn0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIn4">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-NNTP_235-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIn8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIoA">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-NNTP_235-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIoE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIoI">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-NNTP-235" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NNTP" title="NNTP" class="mw-redirect" id="mwIoM">NNTP</a> support can be added by installing the add-on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/InfoRSS?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="InfoRSS (page does not exist)" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" id="mwIoQ" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["InfoRSS"]}}'>infoRSS</a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ChatZilla-236" id="cite_note-ChatZilla-236" data-mw-footnote-number="g"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIoU"><a href="#cite_ref-ChatZilla_236-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIoY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIoc">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ChatZilla_236-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIog"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIok">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ChatZilla_236-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIoo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIos">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ChatZilla_236-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIow"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIo0">4</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ChatZilla_236-4" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIo4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIo8">5</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ChatZilla_236-5" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIpA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIpE">6</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ChatZilla-236" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">IRC support can be added by installing <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ChatZilla" title="ChatZilla" id="mwIpI">ChatZilla</a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-MozIDN-237" id="cite_note-MozIDN-237" data-mw-footnote-number="h"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIpM"><a href="#cite_ref-MozIDN_237-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIpQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIpU">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozIDN_237-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIpY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIpc">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozIDN_237-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIpg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIpk">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozIDN_237-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIpo"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIps">4</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozIDN_237-4" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIpw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIp0">5</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozIDN_237-5" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIp4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIp8">6</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-MozIDN-237" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">For security reasons, IDN domains are displayed as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punycode" title="Punycode" id="mwIqA">punycode</a> if they contain certain characters or if the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Top-level_domain" title="Top-level domain" id="mwIqE">top-level domain</a> has not been <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whitelist" title="Whitelist" id="mwIqI">whitelisted</a> <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://kb.mozillazine.org/Network.IDN.blacklist_chars" class="external autonumber" id="mwIqM"></a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-firetorrent-238" id="cite_note-firetorrent-238" data-mw-footnote-number="i"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIqQ"><a href="#cite_ref-firetorrent_238-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIqU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIqY">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-firetorrent_238-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIqc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIqg">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-firetorrent_238-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIqk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIqo">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-firetorrent-238" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Possible using third party extensions like FoxTorrent<sup about="#mwt5782" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-245" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-245"}}'><a href="#cite_note-245" id="mwIqs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwIqw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIq0">[</span>111<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIq4">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-DilloSSL-240" id="cite_note-DilloSSL-240" data-mw-footnote-number="j"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIq8"><a href="#cite_ref-DilloSSL_240-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIrA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIrE">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-DilloSSL-240" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Dillo has experimental SSL integration that is by standard turned off. <link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt6393" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwIrI" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" id="mwIrM"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20080509062517/http://www.dillo.org/FAQ.html#q12" class="external text" id="mwIrQ">"How do I enable the https (SSL) support plugin for dillo?"</a>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.dillo.org/FAQ.html#q12" class="external text" id="mwIrU">the original</a> on 9 May 2008<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwIrY">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwIrc">12 April</span> 2017</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=How+do+I+enable+the+https+%28SSL%29+support+plugin+for+dillo%3F&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.dillo.org%2FFAQ.html%23q12&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AComparison+of+web+browsers" class="Z3988" id="mwIrg"></span> There is no certificate caching and <i id="mwIrk">no authentication</i> performed.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-system-wide-241" id="cite_note-system-wide-241" data-mw-footnote-number="k"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIro"><a href="#cite_ref-system-wide_241-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIrs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIrw">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-system-wide_241-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIr0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIr4">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-system-wide_241-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIr8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIsA">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-system-wide_241-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIsE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIsI">4</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-system-wide-241" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Respects system-wide proxy settings.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-FirefoxGopherDropped-244" id="cite_note-FirefoxGopherDropped-244" data-mw-footnote-number="l"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIsM"><a href="#cite_ref-FirefoxGopherDropped_244-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIsQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIsU">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-FirefoxGopherDropped-244" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Firefox support for the Gopher protocol was dropped in Firefox 4 (Gecko 1.9.3) per bug 388195.<sup about="#mwt5766" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-243" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-243"}}'><a href="#cite_note-243" id="mwIsY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwIsc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIsg">[</span>110<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIsk">]</span></span></a></sup> This and newer versions have full Gopher support when the OverbiteFF extension is installed.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IEdataprotocol-250" id="cite_note-IEdataprotocol-250" data-mw-footnote-number="m"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIso"><a href="#cite_ref-IEdataprotocol_250-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIss"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIsw">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IEdataprotocol-250" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Microsoft has limited support to certain "non-navigable" content, such as in <code id="mwIs0">&lt;img></code> tags and CSS rules, for security reasons, including concerns that JavaScript embedded in a data URI may not be interpretable by script filters such as those used by web-based email clients.<sup about="#mwt5900" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-MSDN_249-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"MSDN"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-MSDN-249"}}'><a href="#cite_note-MSDN-249" id="mwIs4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwIs8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwItA">[</span>115<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwItE">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-KonqGopher-251" id="cite_note-KonqGopher-251" data-mw-footnote-number="n"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwItI"><a href="#cite_ref-KonqGopher_251-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwItM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwItQ">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-KonqGopher-251" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Konqueror has full Gopher support when the kgopher KIO plugin is installed.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ns8-252" id="cite_note-ns8-252" data-mw-footnote-number="o"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwItU"><a href="#cite_ref-ns8_252-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwItY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwItc">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ns8_252-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwItg"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwItk">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ns8_252-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIto"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIts">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ns8-252" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Depends on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Browser_engine" title="Browser engine" id="mwItw">layout engine</a> which is chosen: Trident or Gecko.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-OpGopher-255" id="cite_note-OpGopher-255" data-mw-footnote-number="p"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIt0"><a href="#cite_ref-OpGopher_255-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwIt4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIt8">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-OpGopher-255" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Includes a proxy capability for gopher support.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-no-ui-256" id="cite_note-no-ui-256" data-mw-footnote-number="q"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwIuA"><a href="#cite_ref-no-ui_256-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIuE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIuI">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-no-ui_256-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwIuM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwIuQ">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-no-ui-256" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Behavior towards malicious certificates can only be set up in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compiler" title="Compiler" id="mwIuU">compile time</a>.</span></li>
</ol></div></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwIuY" aria-labelledby="Image_format_support"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Image_format_support">Image format support</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Comparison_of_web_browsers&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: Image format support"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwIuc">Information about what image formats the browsers support. External links lead to information about support in future versions of the browsers or extensions that provide such functionality.
