<td style="background: var(--background-color-interactive, #EEE); color: var(--color-base, black); vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; " class="table-Unknown" typeof="mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt7297" id="mwJts" data-mw='{"parts":["| ",{"template":{"target":{"wt":"dunno","href":"./Template:Dunno"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'>?</td>
<td style="background: var(--background-color-interactive, #EEE); color: var(--color-base, black); vertical-align: middle; text-align: center; " class="table-Unknown" typeof="mw:Transclusion" about="#mwt7298" id="mwJtw" data-mw='{"parts":["| ",{"template":{"target":{"wt":"dunno","href":"./Template:Dunno"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'>?</td></tr>
<tr class="sortbottom" id="mwJt0">
<th id="mwJt4">Browser</th>
<th id="mwJt8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JPEG" title="JPEG" id="mwJuA">JPEG</a></th>
<th id="mwJuE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JPEG_2000" title="JPEG 2000" id="mwJuI">JPEG 2000</a></th>
<th id="mwJuM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JPEG_XR" title="JPEG XR" id="mwJuQ">JPEG XR</a></th>
<th id="mwJuU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WebP" title="WebP" id="mwJuY">WebP</a></th>
<th id="mwJuc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GIF" title="GIF" id="mwJug">GIF</a></th>
<th id="mwJuk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PNG" title="PNG" id="mwJuo">PNG</a></th>
<th id="mwJus"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/APNG" title="APNG" id="mwJuw">APNG</a></th>
<th id="mwJu0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TIFF" title="TIFF" id="mwJu4">TIFF</a><sup about="#mwt7299" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-TIFF_257-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"TIFF","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"html":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"TIFF"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-TIFF-257" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJu8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJvA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJvE">[</span>a<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJvI">]</span></span></a></sup></th>
<th id="mwJvM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SVG" title="SVG" id="mwJvQ">SVG</a><sup about="#mwt7302" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-SVG_258-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"SVG","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"html":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"SVG"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-SVG-258" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJvU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJvY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJvc">[</span>b<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJvg">]</span></span></a></sup></th>
<th id="mwJvk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PDF" title="PDF" id="mwJvo">PDF</a><sup about="#mwt7305" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-PDF_260-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"PDF","group":"lower-alpha"},"body":{"html":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"efn","href":"./Template:Efn"},"params":{"name":{"wt":"PDF"}},"i":0}}]}'><a href="#cite_note-PDF-260" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJvs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJvw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJv0">[</span>c<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJv4">]</span></span></a></sup></th>
<th id="mwJv8"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canvas_element" title="Canvas element" id="mwJwA">2D Canvas</a></th>
<th id="mwJwE"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X_BitMap" title="X BitMap" id="mwJwI">XBM</a></th>
<th id="mwJwM"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMP_file_format" title="BMP file format" id="mwJwQ">BMP</a></th>
<th id="mwJwU"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ICO_(file_format)" title="ICO (file format)" id="mwJwY">ICO</a></th>
<th id="mwJwc"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/High_Efficiency_Image_File_Format" title="High Efficiency Image File Format" id="mwJwg">HEIF</a></th></tr>
</tbody></table>

<span class="mw-empty-elt" about="#mwt7308" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwJwk" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"notelist","href":"./Template:Notelist"},"params":{"refs":{"wt":"{{efn|name=lynx|While lacking support for inline display of graphical elements, Lynx allows defining standalone image viewer and assigning programs to [[MIME type]]s. Such program is called when user activates corresponding element, effectively allowing Lynx user to add support for arbitrary non-inlined file format.}}\n{{efn|name=KONQJP2K|Konqueror supports JPEG2000 if KDE&apos;s viewer is compiled with Jasper library.}}\n{{efn|name=IEXBM|Internet Explorer support for XBM files was removed in Version 6.}}\n{{efn|name=IEPNG|Internet Explorer supports PNG images but is unable to correctly display images with [[gamma correction]] or [[color correction]].{{Citation needed|date=January 2011}} Versions of Internet Explorer prior to version 7 are unable to correctly display images with [[alpha compositing|alpha channel]] (for transparency) without additional coding [http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/ms649487.aspx].}}\n&lt;!--MozMNG is declared above because of nested tags-->\n&lt;!--NSMNG is declared above because of nested tags-->\n{{efn|name=TIFF|Although it was one of the first suggested WWW image formats, most browsers support [[Tagged Image File Format|TIFF]] by using a plugin installed by the user instead of decoding it natively.}}\n{{efn|name=SVG|SVG here refers to SVG 1.1 Full. There are also two simplified profiles known as SVG 1.1 Tiny and SVG 1.1 Basic, which are intended for user agents with limited capabilities.}}\n{{efn|name=FFSVG|Firefox and SeaMonkey partially support SVG 1.1 Full. Modules that are implemented or not implemented and details of their implementation: [https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/SVG_in_Firefox].}}\n{{efn|name=SVGT|Opera supports SVG 1.1 Basic.[http://www.opera.com/docs/specs/#graphics] {{Webarchive|url=https://archive.today/20120604/http://www.opera.com/docs/specs/#graphics |date=4 June 2012 }}}}\n&lt;!--WKSVG is declared above because of nested tags-->\n{{efn|name=PDF|Most browsers support [[Portable Document Format|PDF]] by installing an [[Adobe Systems|Adobe]] plugin which takes over the browser window. Listed here are browsers which also support inline PDFs within other [[hypertext]] documents (such as within HTML&apos;s &lt;img/> tag). Note that PDF (in strictly speaking) is not an image format, but a scriptable rich text document format that can contain different types of multimedia content, including [[vector graphics|vector]] and [[raster graphics|bitmap]] graphics, audio, video, forms, intra- and inter-document hypertext links and a hierarchical contents listing. The format is also the native display format under macOS.}}\n{{efn|name=KonqPDF|Inline PDF viewing in Konqueror requires KPDF which is included in kdegraphics.}}\n{{efn|name=IECanvas|Support for the [[canvas element]] was added to Internet Explorer 9. Earlier versions of Internet Explorer can be made to emulate canvas using the [https://code.google.com/p/explorercanvas/ excanvas] script.}}\n{{efn|name=FFXBM|In [[Gecko (layout engine)|Gecko]] 1.9.2 (Firefox 3.6) XBM support was dropped.}}\n{{efn|name=MozAPNG|Mozilla applications rebranded by the [[GNU]] project, such as [[GNU IceCat]] or [[Iceape]] do not support APNG.{{citation needed|date=August 2015}}}}\n{{efn|name=ChroAPNG|For Chromium prior to version 59 there is support via an extension.}}\n{{efn|name=QupSVG|Falkon supports as much SVG specification as WebKit does: [http://www.webkit.org/projects/svg/status.xml].}}\n{{efn|name=OperaAPNG|Opera is currently supporting APNG on their Beta and Dev builds.}}\n{{efn|name=PaleMoonJPEGXR|Pale Moon supports JPEG-XR from the first quarter of 2017. [https://github.com/MoonchildProductions/Pale-Moon/issues/105]}}\n{{efn|name=SafariHEIF|Safari support for HEIF pronounced in 2017 from version 11 on operating systems [[macOS Sierra]] and {{nowrap|iOS 11}}. [https://www.cnet.com/news/apple-answers-iphone-storage-woes-with-smaller-photos-videos/]}}\n{{efn|name=nn-32|32-bit version only.}}\n{{efn|name=ns8|Depends on the [[Browser engine|layout engine]] which is chosen: Trident or Gecko.}}"}},"i":0}}]}'><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1327269900" about="#mwt7309" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Reflist/styles.css"}}'/></span><div about="#mwt7308" id="mwJwo">
<div class="mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns" typeof="mw:Extension/references" about="#mwt7350" id="mwJws" data-mw='{"name":"references","attrs":{"group":"lower-alpha","responsive":"1"},"body":{"extsrc":"{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:887}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:888}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:889}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:890}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:891}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:892}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:893}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:894}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:895}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:896}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:897}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:898}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:899}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:900}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:901}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:902}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:903}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:904}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:905}}\n{{#parsoid\u0000fragment:906}}"}}'><ol class="mw-references references" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJww"><li about="#cite_note-TIFF-257" id="cite_note-TIFF-257" data-mw-footnote-number="a"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJw0"><a href="#cite_ref-TIFF_257-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJw4"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJw8">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-TIFF_257-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJxA"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJxE">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-TIFF-257" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Although it was one of the first suggested WWW image formats, most browsers support <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tagged_Image_File_Format" title="Tagged Image File Format" class="mw-redirect" id="mwJxI">TIFF</a> by using a plugin installed by the user instead of decoding it natively.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-SVG-258" id="cite_note-SVG-258" data-mw-footnote-number="b"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJxM"><a href="#cite_ref-SVG_258-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJxQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJxU">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-SVG_258-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJxY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJxc">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-SVG-258" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">SVG here refers to SVG 1.1 Full. There are also two simplified profiles known as SVG 1.1 Tiny and SVG 1.1 Basic, which are intended for user agents with limited capabilities.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-PDF-260" id="cite_note-PDF-260" data-mw-footnote-number="c"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJxg"><a href="#cite_ref-PDF_260-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJxk"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJxo">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-PDF_260-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJxs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJxw">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-PDF-260" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Most browsers support <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portable_Document_Format" title="Portable Document Format" class="mw-redirect" id="mwJx0">PDF</a> by installing an <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe_Systems" title="Adobe Systems" class="mw-redirect" id="mwJx4">Adobe</a> plugin which takes over the browser window. Listed here are browsers which also support inline PDFs within other <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hypertext" title="Hypertext" id="mwJx8">hypertext</a> documents (such as within HTML's &lt;img /> tag). Note that PDF (in strictly speaking) is not an image format, but a scriptable rich text document format that can contain different types of multimedia content, including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vector_graphics" title="Vector graphics" id="mwJyA">vector</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raster_graphics" title="Raster graphics" id="mwJyE">bitmap</a> graphics, audio, video, forms, intra- and inter-document hypertext links and a hierarchical contents listing. The format is also the native display format under macOS.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IEPNG-261" id="cite_note-IEPNG-261" data-mw-footnote-number="d"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJyI"><a href="#cite_ref-IEPNG_261-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJyM"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJyQ">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-IEPNG_261-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJyU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJyY">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IEPNG-261" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Internet Explorer supports PNG images but is unable to correctly display images with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamma_correction" title="Gamma correction" id="mwJyc">gamma correction</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Color_correction" title="Color correction" id="mwJyg">color correction</a>.<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" id="mwJyk"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_January_2011" id="mwJyo"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" id="mwJys"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwJyw">[</span><i id="mwJy0"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed" id="mwJy4"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (January 2011)" id="mwJy8">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwJzA">]</span></sup> Versions of Internet Explorer prior to version 7 are unable to correctly display images with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpha_compositing" title="Alpha compositing" id="mwJzE">alpha channel</a> (for transparency) without additional coding <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/ms649487.aspx" class="external autonumber" id="mwJzI"></a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IECanvas-262" id="cite_note-IECanvas-262" data-mw-footnote-number="e"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJzM"><a href="#cite_ref-IECanvas_262-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJzQ"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJzU">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-IECanvas_262-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJzY"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJzc">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IECanvas-262" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Support for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canvas_element" title="Canvas element" id="mwJzg">canvas element</a> was added to Internet Explorer 9. Earlier versions of Internet Explorer can be made to emulate canvas using the <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://code.google.com/p/explorercanvas/" class="external text" id="mwJzk">excanvas</a> script.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-IEXBM-263" id="cite_note-IEXBM-263" data-mw-footnote-number="f"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJzo"><a href="#cite_ref-IEXBM_263-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJzs"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJzw">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-IEXBM_263-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJz0"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJz4">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-IEXBM_263-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJz8"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ0A">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-IEXBM-263" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Internet Explorer support for XBM files was removed in Version 6.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-FFSVG-264" id="cite_note-FFSVG-264" data-mw-footnote-number="g"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ0E"><a href="#cite_ref-FFSVG_264-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJ0I"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ0M">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-FFSVG_264-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJ0Q"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ0U">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-FFSVG_264-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJ0Y"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ0c">3</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-FFSVG_264-3" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJ0g"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ0k">4</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-FFSVG-264" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Firefox and SeaMonkey partially support SVG 1.1 Full. Modules that are implemented or not implemented and details of their implementation: <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/SVG_in_Firefox" class="external autonumber" id="mwJ0o"></a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ChroAPNG-266" id="cite_note-ChroAPNG-266" data-mw-footnote-number="h"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ0s"><a href="#cite_ref-ChroAPNG_266-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJ0w"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ00">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ChroAPNG_266-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJ04"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ08">2</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-ChroAPNG_266-2" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJ1A"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ1E">3</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ChroAPNG-266" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">For Chromium prior to version 59 there is support via an extension.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-QupSVG-268" id="cite_note-QupSVG-268" data-mw-footnote-number="i"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ1I"><a href="#cite_ref-QupSVG_268-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwJ1M"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ1Q">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-QupSVG-268" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Falkon supports as much SVG specification as WebKit does: <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.webkit.org/projects/svg/status.xml" class="external autonumber" id="mwJ1U"></a>.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-MozAPNG-272" id="cite_note-MozAPNG-272" data-mw-footnote-number="j"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ1Y"><a href="#cite_ref-MozAPNG_272-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJ1c"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ1g">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-MozAPNG_272-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJ1k"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ1o">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-MozAPNG-272" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Mozilla applications rebranded by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU" title="GNU" id="mwJ1s">GNU</a> project, such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GNU_IceCat" title="GNU IceCat" id="mwJ1w">GNU IceCat</a> or <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iceape" title="Iceape" class="mw-redirect" id="mwJ10">Iceape</a> do not support APNG.<link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements" id="mwJ14"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_August_2015" id="mwJ18"/><sup class="noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact" style="white-space:nowrap;" id="mwJ2A"><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwJ2E">[</span><i id="mwJ2I"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed" title="Wikipedia:Citation needed" id="mwJ2M"><span title="This claim needs references to reliable sources. (August 2015)" id="mwJ2Q">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwJ2U">]</span></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-FFXBM-274" id="cite_note-FFXBM-274" data-mw-footnote-number="k"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ2Y"><a href="#cite_ref-FFXBM_274-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwJ2c"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ2g">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-FFXBM-274" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">In <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gecko_(layout_engine)" title="Gecko (layout engine)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwJ2k">Gecko</a> 1.9.2 (Firefox 3.6) XBM support was dropped.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-KONQJP2K-276" id="cite_note-KONQJP2K-276" data-mw-footnote-number="l"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ2o"><a href="#cite_ref-KONQJP2K_276-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwJ2s"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ2w">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-KONQJP2K-276" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Konqueror supports JPEG2000 if KDE's viewer is compiled with Jasper library.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-KonqPDF-277" id="cite_note-KonqPDF-277" data-mw-footnote-number="m"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ20"><a href="#cite_ref-KonqPDF_277-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwJ24"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ28">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-KonqPDF-277" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Inline PDF viewing in Konqueror requires KPDF which is included in kdegraphics.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-lynx-278" id="cite_note-lynx-278" data-mw-footnote-number="n"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ3A"><a href="#cite_ref-lynx_278-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJ3E"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ3I">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-lynx_278-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJ3M"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ3Q">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-lynx-278" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">While lacking support for inline display of graphical elements, Lynx allows defining standalone image viewer and assigning programs to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MIME_type" title="MIME type" class="mw-redirect" id="mwJ3U">MIME types</a>. Such program is called when user activates corresponding element, effectively allowing Lynx user to add support for arbitrary non-inlined file format.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-WKSVG-279" id="cite_note-WKSVG-279" data-mw-footnote-number="o"><span rel="mw:referencedBy" class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ3Y"><a href="#cite_ref-WKSVG_279-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJ3c"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ3g">1</span></a> <a href="#cite_ref-WKSVG_279-1" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" id="mwJ3k"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ3o">2</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-WKSVG-279" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Safari 3 is able to render SVG documents, but not fully.<sup about="#mwt7143" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-285" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-285"}}'><a href="#cite_note-285" id="mwJ3s"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJ3w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJ30">[</span>126<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJ34">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-ns8-280" id="cite_note-ns8-280" data-mw-footnote-number="p"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ38"><a href="#cite_ref-ns8_280-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwJ4A"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ4E">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-ns8-280" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Depends on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Browser_engine" title="Browser engine" id="mwJ4I">layout engine</a> which is chosen: Trident or Gecko.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-nn-32-281" id="cite_note-nn-32-281" data-mw-footnote-number="q"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ4M"><a href="#cite_ref-nn-32_281-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwJ4Q"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ4U">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-nn-32-281" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">32-bit version only.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-OperaAPNG-282" id="cite_note-OperaAPNG-282" data-mw-footnote-number="r"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ4Y"><a href="#cite_ref-OperaAPNG_282-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwJ4c"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ4g">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-OperaAPNG-282" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Opera is currently supporting APNG on their Beta and Dev builds.</span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-SVGT-283" id="cite_note-SVGT-283" data-mw-footnote-number="s"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ4k"><a href="#cite_ref-SVGT_283-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwJ4o"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ4s">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-SVGT-283" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Opera supports SVG 1.1 Basic.<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="http://www.opera.com/docs/specs/#graphics" class="external autonumber" id="mwJ4w"></a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Archive.today_guidance" title="Wikipedia:Archive.today guidance" id="mwJ40">Deprecated link</a> archived 4 June 2012<span style="font-size:100%" class="error citation-comment" id="mwJ44"><sup id="mwJ48">(Timestamp length)</sup></span> at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Archive.today" title="Archive.today" id="mwJ5A">archive.today</a><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Webarchive_template_archiveis_links" id="mwJ5E"/><link rel="mw:PageProp/Category" href="./Category:Webarchive_template_warnings" id="mwJ5I"/></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-PaleMoonJPEGXR-284" id="cite_note-PaleMoonJPEGXR-284" data-mw-footnote-number="t"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ5M"><a href="#cite_ref-PaleMoonJPEGXR_284-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwJ5Q"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ5U">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-PaleMoonJPEGXR-284" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Pale Moon supports JPEG-XR from the first quarter of 2017. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://github.com/MoonchildProductions/Pale-Moon/issues/105" class="external autonumber" id="mwJ5Y"></a></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-SafariHEIF-286" id="cite_note-SafariHEIF-286" data-mw-footnote-number="u"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ5c"><a href="#cite_ref-SafariHEIF_286-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwJ5g"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ5k">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-SafariHEIF-286" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">Safari support for HEIF pronounced in 2017 from version 11 on operating systems <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MacOS_Sierra" title="MacOS Sierra" id="mwJ5o">macOS Sierra</a> and <span class="nowrap" id="mwJ5s">iOS 11</span>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.cnet.com/news/apple-answers-iphone-storage-woes-with-smaller-photos-videos/" class="external autonumber" id="mwJ5w"></a></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-CairoPDF-287" id="cite_note-CairoPDF-287" data-mw-footnote-number="v"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwJ50"><a href="#cite_ref-CairoPDF_287-0" data-mw-group="lower-alpha" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwJ54"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwJ58">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-CairoPDF-287" class="mw-reference-text reference-text" data-mw-group="lower-alpha">With the addition of the new <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cairo_(graphics)" title="Cairo (graphics)" id="mwJ6A">Cairo</a> version in Gecko 1.9 it will be natively possible to save pages to PDFs but not read them. This feature is not included in Firefox 3.5, however it is possible with the new Cairo backend.</span></li>
</ol></div></div>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwJ6E" aria-labelledby="Internationalization"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Internationalization">Internationalization</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Comparison_of_web_browsers&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: Internationalization"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwJ6I">Most browsers are available in more than one language.
